hadiths[1002]{hadithnumber,text}:
"23047","(23047) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Abu Qurayh, on the authority of Salman bin Rabi’ah. Al-Bahili: Concerning a man who bought goods from another man with the expectation that he would look at them, and he paid the price, and she died, so Salman bin Spring"
"23048","(23048) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer: Concerning a man who buys goods on the condition that he waits. To her and she died. He said: The buyer guarantees it."
"23049","(23049) Waki’ told us, he said: Hammad bin Zayd told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Ateeq, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: He guarantees The buyer, if he has the option."
"23050","(23050) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan: He used to say: If a man buys goods with the understanding that they are in it, With the option, then he has it from him. He said: If he named the price, then he is a guarantor. If he did not name the price, then he is liable. Therein is trustworthy."
"23051","(23051) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Layla used to say: If the seller had the option and the commodity died, then there is no The buyer has something to do.\n Sufyan said: He guarantees the value."
"23052","(23052) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer: Concerning a man who says to another man: Do you have a witness? He says: No, then he comes and bears witness. He says: It is permissible."
"23053","(23053) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Muhammad, who said: Al-Qasim bin Muhammad bore witness with Aban bin Othman to a man, so the man made his mention of something in his testimony, so he said: I do not remember him, nor do I remember anything except this, then he left. So he mentioned while the people were sitting, and he said: This man asked me something about a testimony that I had not mentioned to him, but I have mentioned it. And I bear witness that what he said is true, and I bear witness to it."
"23054","(23054) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Masoud: He was reluctant to sell Offices"
"23055","(23055) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, or on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: There is no harm in being sold. If there is anything left of him, he must write to someone who buys him and guarantees his emancipation, and does not sell him into slavery."
"23056","(23056) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha: that Burayra came to her and A letter, so I asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: Did he buy her on the condition that her loyalty is to her master? He said: Buy her and free her, for loyalty belongs to the one who frees her.\n(Bukhari 2563, Muslim 1143)"
"23057","(23057) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Abi Malika informed me: A woman wrote She gave birth to two sons during her correspondence, then she died, and Abdullah bin Al-Zubair was asked about that? He said: If they abide by their mother’s letter, that is for them, so if they fulfill it, they will be freed."
"23058","(23058) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The children of the Muqatabah are in her position, they will be freed. By freeing her, they will be freed from her, and if she dies, they will do what remains of her correspondence. If they pay, they will be freed, and if they are unable, they will be enslaved."
"23059","(23059) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, who said: His son is in the same position as you in striving. Meaning: correspondence."
"23060","(23060) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Hijr al-Madri, on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, made the Omri inheritance for the heir. (Abu Dawud 3554, An-Nasa’i 6552)"
"23061","(23061) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Yassar: that Tariq ruled that Al-Amri should be given to the heir, according to the saying Jaber on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Muslim 1247)"
"23062","(23062) Ibn Abi Zaydah narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: No, my life is mine. Whoever makes something, it is his. (Ibn Majah 2379. An-Nasa’i 6584)"
"23063","(23063) Ibn Abi Zaydah narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Tawoos, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Umri is permissible for the one who made it `Umrah. (Ahmad 1/250)"
"23064","(23064) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Omri is an inheritance for her family or a reward for her family. (Tirmidhi 1349, Abu Dawud 3544)"
"23065","(23065) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Keep your property and do not inhabit it, for whoever gives my life to him is by inheritance.\n(Muslim 27 Ahmad 3/302)"
"23066","(23066) Waki’ told us, he said: Hisham bin Urwah told us, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And peace be upon him: Whoever extends my life, it belongs to him and to his heirs after him."
"23067","(23067) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Omri is an inheritance. (Nasa’i 6546. Ahmad 5/189)"
"23068","(23068) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, he said: Salma bin Kuhayl informed us, he said: We were sitting at Sharih: When a people came to him disputing about my life, I assigned to a man his life, and he said: To him is his life and his death. Then the one who had judged him came to him and appealed to him, and Shurayh said: This man blamed me for a matter that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had decided. May God bless him and grant him peace."
"23069","(23069) Abu Osama narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, on the authority of Makhoul, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: Whichever man’s life is given to him, and he can do with it what he wants."
"23070","(23070) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Ibn al-Hanafi, on the authority of Ali, who said: Al-Amri At times"
"23071","(23071) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: He came to him A Bedouin said: I gave my nephew a female camel, and it grew until it became a camel, so what do you think of it? He said: To Him belongs His life and death. The Bedouin said: You have only made it a charity. He said: That is farther away from it for you than it is."
"23072","(23072) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, he said: I asked Ibrahim about the dwelling place? He said: It is returned to the heirs of the dwelling, so I said: O Abu Imran, wasn’t it said: Whoever owns something for his life, it belongs to him His life and death? He said: That is in Al-Umari."
"23073","(23073) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman bin Ghayath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: I heard him say: If a man gives another man the house His life is his life and after his death."
"23074","(23074) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Jarir bin Hazim narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: A blind man came to him. He was disputing about a mother who had taken care of her, and a judge was given over to her by the one who took care of her. The man said: You have judged me. He said: I have not judged. On you, but the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, decided: Whoever owns something for its life, it is his for its life and its death.\n(Bayhaqi 1750; Abd al-Razzaq 14880)"
"23075","(23075) Waki’ told us, he said: Ibn Abi Khalid told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’biy, he said: If he says, “Your life is yours,” then he has a life. And his death"
"23076","(23076) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Who was appointed My life is for him and his heirs."
"23077","(23077) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj bin Abi Uthman narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: O people of Ansar, keep your property and do not inhabit it, for he is the one who inhabited it. Whatever it is, it belongs to the one who commanded it. (Muslim 27 Ahmad 3/317)"
"23078","(23078) Ali told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, he said: I heard Muawiyah saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Umri is permissible for her family.\n(Ahmad 4/97, Abu Ali 7331)"
"23079","(23079) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Jabir, He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, decided the lifespan for him and his successor, and the one who gave him had no conditions or Twofold\n(Bukhari 2425. Muslim 1246)"
"23080","(23080) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of An-Nadr bin Anas, on the authority of Bashir bin Naykah. On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Omri is permissible for her family or inheritance. To her family.\n(Muslim 32. Ahmad 2/468)"
"23081","(23081) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Hammad, that they said: The companion of Al-Umri will return as long as Ḥayyin"
"23082","(23082) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Yazid bin Ziyad bin Abi Al-Ja’d narrated to us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the necking of necks, and he said: Whoever necks my neck will have it for him. (An-Nasa’i) 6566"
"23083","(23083) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Hanzala narrated to us, on the authority of Tawus, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: It is not permissible The sergeant, whoever serges my sergeant, it is for the sake of inheritance. (Abu Dawud 3554; Abd al-Razzaq 16913)"
"23084","(23084) Ibn Ali told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Tawus, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: No my neck, he who keeps my neck. For the heirs of Al-Marqab."
"23085","(23085) Waki’ told us, he said: Shuabi told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: Ali said: Al-Amri And the neck is the same."
"23086","(23086) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sa`id bin Hassan narrated to us, saying: I heard Mujahid saying: Whoever gives my life will be his. And its heirs after him will not return to the one who inhabited it, and the raqbi is like it. I said to Mujahid: What is the raqbi? He said: The man’s saying: This is for the other, from me and from you."
"23087","(23087) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Al-Ruqabi and Al-Amri are the same. Wakee’ said: Al-Amri, Al-Hibi, Al-Atiyya, and Al-Nahl, if they are caught, are permissible."
"23088","(23088) Waki’ told us, he said: Ibn Abi Layla told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of May God bless him and grant him peace on the authority of stallions. (Ahmad 2/299, Darmi 2623)"
"23089","(23089) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham Abi Kulayb, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Na’am, On the authority of Abu Saeed, he said: He forbade the honey of a stallion."
"23090","(23090) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Muadh, he said: I was desperate, and Al-Baraa’ shunned me from being unmarried."
"23091","(23091) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: It is unlawful to strike a stallion. And the dowry of a transgressor and the earnings of cuppers."
"23092","(23092) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade And peace be upon him on the path of the stallion. (Muslim 1197. An-Nasa’i 6266)"
"23093","(23093) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Walid bin Issa Al-Saadi narrated to us, saying: I said to Al-Hasan: We have goats that we rent. He said: There is nothing wrong with it as long as it is not milked or milked."
"23094","(23094) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: You do not take a wage for the one who beats a stallion, and that is okay. To give if you do not find anyone to encourage you."
"23095","(23095) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Al-Musayyab bin Rafi’, he said: They used to enter Alqamiya while he was He drives his sheep, that is, he takes the goat out on them, feeds them, and milks them."
"23096","(23096) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: What is measured is not safe in what is measured, nor is what is handed over. It is weighed as it is weighed."
"23097","(23097) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abdullah bin Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: Do not hand over food. In food, nor in meat in meat, and he did not see any harm in serving food in the standing tea."
"23098","(23098) Ibn Abi Za’idah told us, on the authority of Ibn Salem, he said: Al-Sha’bi said: Do not buy anything that will be measured for something that will be equal to it. Until later"
"23099","(23099) Abdul-Wahhab bin Ata’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of Al-Hasan and his followers: They both disliked that He delivers food to food."
"23100","(23100) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no harm in someone being delivered. It is measured according to what it is measured, and what is weighed according to what is weighed is food for food."
"23101","(23101) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’: Concerning a man who pays to another man speculative money. A guarantor. He said: There is no guarantor."
"23102","(23102) Muhammad bin Sawa’i narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: Every condition is in Mudarab. So it is usury, and this is the saying of his leaders."
"23103","(23103) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan: He was asked about a man who paid speculative money to a man and guaranteed it for him. He said: The profit is between them, and he does not pay attention to its guarantee."
"23104","(23104) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, he said: Omar Ibn Al-Khattab said: If a polytheist has a slaveholding and he converts to Islam, it will be taken away. Some of it was sold to Muslims and its price was returned to its owner."
"23105","(23105) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz: He used to order the sale of the slaves of non-Muslims if they converted to Islam."
"23106","(23106) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If the mother of a Christian’s child converts to Islam, she seeks her value, and when The mother he sold converted to Islam."
"23107","(23107) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If a slave of the dhimmi converts to Islam, he will be dispersed. Between him and his master."
"23108","(23108) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, saying: Whoever is one of your fatwas and converts to Islam, then he is free, and he is not free. They bought from the captive Muslims, so he converted to Islam. He was sold among the Muslims."
"23109","(23109) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Rabi’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If a slave of a dhimmi converts to Islam, he is brought up to the imam and he sells him for it. Muslims, and paid its price to his master. Al-Hasan said: A Muslim should not serve an infidel."
"23110","(23110) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: The Sunnah has passed, that an infidel should not be enslaved. Muslim"
"23111","(23111) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim: {And do not wish to increase.} He said: Do not give in order to increase."
"23112","(23112) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’abi, he said: narrated to me someone who heard Ikrimah say: Do not give a gift if you want to It takes more than her."
"23113","(23113) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Salama bin Nabit, on the authority of Ad-Dahhak: {And do not wish in abundance.} He said: Do not give in order to be given. More than that"
"23114","(23114) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Rawwad, who said: I heard al-Dahhak: {And you have not given usury that they may raise money. people, so they do not trust in the sight of God.} He said: This was exclusively for the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"23115","(23115) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Al-Hasan: In his saying: {And do not wish to increase.} He said: Do not entrust your work to usury so that you may be too great for your Lord."
"23116","(23116) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abi Bazza, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umrafi, who said: {And do not You are too much. He said: Do not give something in order to ask for more of it."
"23117","(23117) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour bin Safiyyah, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, who said: The man He is given so that he may be rewarded, {And whatever usury you have given usury so that they may profit from the wealth of people, it will not increase in the sight of Allah}"
"23118","(23118) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Gifts."
"23119","(23119) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The man used to give his relatives So that his wealth may increase thereby."
"23120","(23120) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ikrimah, {And whatever usury you give us so that they may profit from people’s wealth, it will not be They are sought in the sight of God."
"23121","(23121) Abd al-Salam told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no permission for the market stalls."
"23122","(23122) Hafs, Ibn Aliyah, and Abd al-Salam narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, who said: If a driver opens his door and sits down, he then"
"23123","(23123) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, he said: Ibrahim al-Taymi, Ibrahim al-Nakha’i, and Khaythamah were Our companions come to us in the market shops and do nothing more than say: Peace be upon you, then they enter."
"23124","(23124) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Ikrimah: It was said to him: Ibn Umar used to ask permission to On the market shops? He said: Who can endure what Ibn Omar could endure?"
"23125","(23125) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: Ibn Sirin used to come to me in Hijra Bari and say: :Peace be upon you, then he enters."
"23126","(23126) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Shuaib, who said: Abu Al Ali used to come to Bari’s house and say: Peace be upon him. Is it upon you? So I say: May God have mercy on you, but it is the market, and he says: The man may have neglected his account, and perhaps he has neglected to inspect the dirhams."
"23127","(23127) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: I was with Mujahid in the Kufa market and there were tents for the tailors. He was approaching the market next to the turn of Banu al-Baka', and he said: Ibn Umar used to ask for permission in something like this. He said: And I said: How?"
"23128","(23128) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Ubad ibn Muslim al-Fazari narrated to us, on the authority of Abi Ubaid al-Muharbibi’s dirhams, he said: I saw Ali being struck by the sky while he was in the market, so he took shade in the Persian tent, and the Persian made the Persian push him away. His tent and Ali began to say: I am only seeking shade from the rain. The Persian was later informed that it was Ali, so he began to beat his chest."
"23129","(23129) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, on the authority of Shurayh: that he permitted two female witnesses to be freed."
"23130","(23130) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shurayh: He permitted two women to bear witness in Emancipation, one of them is my uncle. It means: there is a man with them."
"23131","(23131) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: It is permissible for women to be witnesses. Concerning emancipation, debt, and wills. Meaning: with the man."
"23132","(23132) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Shurayh: that he used to permit Witness of women in rights."
"23133","(23133) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhul, who said: It is not permissible for women to witness except in Religion"
"23134","(23134) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: He permits female witnesses."
"23135","(23135) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, saying: Your testimony is permissible in religion and in what is necessary. From him"
"23136","(23136) Waki’ told us, he said: Ismail bin Abi Khaled told us, he said: Al-Mughirah bin Sa’id Al-Sha’abi asked: Should I get married? What is the testimony of the man and the two women in the divorce? He said: Yes."
"23137","(23137) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Jarir bin Hazim narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Al-Kharit, on the authority of Abu Labid: that Omar He permitted women’s witnesses in divorce."
"23138","(23138) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Omar bin Rashid, on the authority of Abu Kathir al-Hanafi, on the authority of Abu Hurairah: He hated it. To sell his fruit and renounce charity."
"23139","(23139) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, who said: He who Honesty"
"23140","(23140) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If you sell your fruit or the fruit of your garden, Charity is within the wall.\n Ibn Abi Malika said: It is on the purchased item."
"23141","(23141) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: The best of what a man eats is from his own earnings, and his children are from his own earnings.\n(Ahmad 6/42, Ibn Hibban 4261)"
"23142","(23142) Ibn Abi Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Mundakir: That a man disputed with his father about... Wealth that he had taken to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: You and your father’s wealth belong to you. (Ibn Majah 2291)"
"23143","(23143) Khalaf bin Khalifa told us, on the authority of Muharib bin Dathar, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A child is one who earns money. The father (Tabarani 5132)"
"23144","(23144) Waki’ and Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Amara bin Umair Al-Laythi, on the authority of his mother, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A man’s children are from what he earns, from the best things he earns.\n(Abu Dawud 3523, Ahmed 126)"
"23145","(23145) Ibn Abi Zaydah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ammar bin Ummar, on the authority of his paternal aunt, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet May God bless him and grant him peace, similarly. (Tirmidhi 1358 and Ahmad 162)"
"23146","(23146) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Suwayd bin Ghafli, on the authority of Aisha, she said: A man may eat from his son’s wealth whatever he wants, and a child may not eat from his father’s wealth except with his permission."
"23147","(23147) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Dawud bin Abdullah narrated to us, saying: I heard Al-Sha’abi saying: Aisha said: The man was born from He earned it, he can eat from his wealth whatever he wants."
"23148","(23148) Waki’ told us, he said: Ibn Abi Layla told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: A man from the Ansar came to the Prophet and prayed. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: O Messenger of God, my father has usurped my property. He said: You and your father’s property."
"23149","(23149) Ibn Abi Zaydah narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, who said: The father eats From his child’s wealth he can take whatever he wants, and a child should not eat from his father’s wealth except of his own accord."
"23150","(23150) Ibn Abi Za’idah and Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, the same."
"23151","(23151) Ibn Abi Zaydi narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir, the same."
"23152","(23152) Ibn Abi Zayed told us, on the authority of Salih bin Hayy, on the authority of Amer, who said: A man is free from his son’s wealth."
"23153","(23153) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Hisham bin Urwah narrated to us, on the authority of his father, he said: A man made anything with his wealth and did not He asked his father’s permission. Hisham said: My father said: So he asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, or Abu Bakr, or Omar, and he said: Return it to him, for it is an arrow from your quiver. (Abdul Razzaq 14627)"
"23154","(23154) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, who said: There was a giving person who saw no harm in a man taking from his son’s wealth. It is not necessary."
"23155","(23155) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Masruq, who said: You are from God’s gift to your father. You and your father’s property. Then he recited: {He grants females to whomever He wishes, and He grants males to whomever He wishes}."
"23156","(23156) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather: that a man came The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: O Messenger of God, my father invaded my wealth, so he said: You and your father’s wealth belong to you.\n(Abu Dawud 3524. Ahmad 2/204)"
"23157","(23157) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: The son must be kind to his father. And every human being is more worthy of what he has."
"23158","(23158) Ibn Abi Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: A man said to Al-Qasim bin Muhammad: Does a man squeeze some money? His son whatever he wants? He said: I don’t know what this is?"
"23159","(23159) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Uthman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid: He said, “Take from your child’s wealth what you give him.” And do not take from him what you have not given him."
"23160","(23160) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Yunus bin Yazid, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem: Hamza bin Abdullah bin Omar slaughtered a camel, and a beggar came and asked Ibn Omar, and Abdullah said: What’s wrong with you? Hamza said: Father, you are free, so eat from it whatever you want."
"23161","(23161) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Mu’ammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: A man spends from his son’s wealth if he is in need. As much as he spent on it."
"23162","(23162) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-A’la, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Han?fiyy, on the authority of Ali, who said: A man has more right to his son’s money when he is young, but when he grows up and takes possession of his money, he has more right to it."
"23163","(23163) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, a man said to Jabir ibn Zayd: My father deprives me of his wealth, saying: No. I will give you some of it. He said: Eat of your father’s wealth on a reasonable basis."
"23164","(23164) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ali and Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of God decided May God bless him and grant him peace, through intercession for neighbors."
"23165","(23165) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of those who heard Ali, and Abdullah, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, decided to be virtuous. (Nasa’i 6304; Abd al-Razzaq 14383)"
"23166","(23166) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Misra, on the authority of Amr ibn al-Sharid, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, who reported To the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: The neighbor has more right to his charity. (Bukhari 6977, Abu Dawud 3510)"
"23167","(23167) Abd bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his commanders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: The neighbor of the house has more right to the house. (Abu Dawud 3511. Ahmad 5/12)"
"23168","(23168) Abduh narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The neighbor has more right to his neighbor’s intercession if their path is the same and he is expected to do so, even if he is absent.\n(Abu Dawud 3512. Ahmad 3/303)"
"23169","(23169) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Al-Mughirah Al-Thaqafi, who said: I heard Al-Sha’bi say: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: The intercessor is more worthy than the neighbor, and the neighbor is more worthy than the neighbour. (Abdul Razzaq 14390)"
"23170","(23170) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Omar bin Rashid Al-Sulami told us, he said: I heard Al-Sha’abi say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, decided to be virtuous. (Abdul Razzaq 14384)"
"23171","(23171) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Hafs: that Omar wrote to Shurayh: He judged the neighborhood. He said: So Shurayh used to judge a man from the people of Kufa over a man from the people of Syria."
"23172","(23172) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: A mixture is more worthy than an intercessor, and an intercessor is more worthy than a neighbor. The neighbor is more worthy than anyone else."
"23173","(23173) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A partner has more right to pre-emption, if he does not have it. A partner and a neighbor."
"23174","(23174) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Amr, on the authority of Fudayl bin Amr, on the authority of Ibrahim, He said: A mixed person is more worthy than a neighbor, and a neighbor is more worthy than someone else."
"23175","(23175) Muawiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, on the authority of his father: That Amr bin Harith He used to judge the neighbourhood."
"23176","(23176) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hussein Al-Mu’allim, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Sharid, on the authority of his father, He said: I said: O Messenger of God, a land in which no one has an oath or any association except the neighbours. He said: The neighbors are more deserving of his punishment whatever he is. \n(Ibn Majah 2496. Tahawi 124)"
"23177","(23177) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Whoever has a partner in land or a quarter does not have the right to sell until he obtains permission from his partner. If he wants, he can take it, and if he wants, he can leave it. (Muslim 1229. Abu Dawud 3507)"
"23178","(23178) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Al-Shafi’i is for the polytheist and the Bedouins. And others.\n Al-Sha’bi said: There is no intercessor for a Bedouin, nor for a polytheist."
"23179","(23179) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Muhajir, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Not for Bedouins, nor for those who do not live in Egypt. Intercession"
"23180","(23180) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Neither the Jew nor the Christian Intercession"
"23181","(23181) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Jarir bin Hazim narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Miqdam Abi Farwa, who said: A neighbor of mine narrated to me: Shurayh ruled that a Christian should be pre-empted."
"23182","(23182) Waki’ narrated to us, Qais bin Al-Rabi’ narrated to us, on the authority of Khaled Al-Hadha’, he said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote: The Jew and Christian have intercession."
"23183","(23183) Hassan bin Saleh told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: He is neither a Jew nor a Christian. Intercession"
"23184","(23184) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us: The Jew and the Christian have intercessors."
"23185","(23185) Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He did not see any intercession for the infidels."
"23186","(23186) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: The Bedouins have intercessors."
"23187","(23187) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Hikam, he said: The Bedouins have Shafi’i, Waki’ said: He said to him: “My intercession.”"
"23188","(23188) Waki’ narrated to us, he said: Zakaria narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: There is no intercession for the Bedouins."
"23189","(23189) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Ash’u’, who said: The Bedouins have no intercessors."
"23190","(23190) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Malik bin Anas, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab and Abu Salama, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ruled for pre-emption for everything that was not divided, so if the legal limits have occurred, then there is no pre-emption.\n(Ibn Majah 2497. Malik 1)"
"23191","(23191) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Amara, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, on the authority of Aban ibn Othman, he said: Othman said: There is no pre-emption for a well, nor for a stallion, and the arf severes all pre-emption."
"23192","(23192) Zaid bin Harun told us, saying: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Aoun bin Ubaid Allah bin Abi Rafi’, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah, who said: Omar bin Al-Khattab said: If the borders are established and the people know their borders, then there is no intercessor. Between them."
"23193","(23193) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Iyas bin Muawiyah: He used to judge the neighborhood until The letter of Omar bin Abdul Aziz came to him stating that it should not be decided unless it was of two mixed partners, or the house should be closed. There is one chapter on her."
"23194","(23194) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Al-Zubayr ibn Musa informed me, on the authority of Omar ibn Abdul Aziz, He said: If the earth is divided, united, and its paths are divided, then there is no intercession."
"23195","(23195) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Aoun bin Ubaid Allah bin Abi Rafi’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah bin Omar said: Omar said: If the punishments are imposed and the people know their rights, then there will be no intercessors among them."
"23196","(23196) Abdul Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: If there is a path between the two lands, then there is no intercessor. Between them."
"23197","(23197) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Ubaid, who said: I heard Abraham say: If there is a dividing road between them There is no intercession."
"23198","(23198) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about pre-emption? He said: If the house is next to the house and there is no road between them, then there is pre-emption in it."
"23199","(23199) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no intercessor except in matters of upbringing."
"23200","(23200) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: There is no intercession except in the case of a jarib or A drug"
"23201","(23201) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of `Ubaydah, on the authority of Abraham: He used to say that."
"23202","(23202) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malika, who said: The Messenger of God decided May God bless him and grant him peace, through pre-emption in everything: the land, the house, the maidservant, and the servant.\n He said: Then he said: Ataa: The pre-emption is only for the land and the house. He said: Ibn Abi Malika said: Do you listen to me? You have no mother! I say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, and then you say something like this? (Tirmidhi 1371, Bayhaqi 109)"
"23203","(23203) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: About the neighbor of the house if they are both in the neighbourhood. Whichever of the above is more deserving of pre-emption."
"23204","(23204) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Yunus bin Abi Ishaq narrated to us, saying: I heard Al-Sha’bi saying: Whoever is sold, I will intercede for him. He is a witness who does not deny it, so there is no intercession for him."
"23205","(23205) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir and Al-Qasim: Concerning a man whose house was sold and he He is silent and does not deny it. They said: It is necessary for him and it is permissible for him."
"23206","(23206) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir and al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman that they were They say to the buyer: Establish proof that it was sold and he is a witness who cannot deny it."
"23207","(23207) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: If the intercessor gives permission for the buyer to purchase So he bought it, but there was no intercession for him."
"23208","(23208) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan said: He has pre-emption because his right occurred after the sale."
"23209","(23209) Ismail Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Taymiyy, on the authority of Abu Uthman: That Ibn Masoud used to hate it if he He lent dirhams in order to take something better from them."
"23210","(23210) Ibn Abi Zayed told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Ibn Umar used to borrow, and when his contribution came out, he would give him something better than it."
"23211","(23211) Qatari bin Abdullah Abu Murri told us, on the authority of Ash’ath Al-Hadani, who said: I asked Al-Hasan and said: O Abu Sa’id, The elders come and I have female neighbors who are generous, and they borrow from me, and my intention is to replace the dirhams of the gift over mine? He said: There is no harm in it."
"23212","(23212) Ibn Abi Zaydi told us, on the authority of Zakaria, who said: I said to Amir: A man borrows, so when his contribution goes out He gave me something better than her. He said: There is no problem as long as you do not stipulate or give him something. I seek that."
"23213","(23213) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: If you borrow something and pay for something better than it, there is no problem. If there is no condition when making the loan."
"23214","(23214) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Hammad, who said: I asked them about a man who lends dirhams to a man. So he takes better than what he gave, and they said: If he did not intend, then there is no problem."
"23215","(23215) Rawad bin Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i: Concerning a man who lent a man ten dirhams, and he brought back ten dirhams. He said: Do not accept it. I said to him: Indeed, his soul was at ease. He said: Is there usury that is the most effective if his soul is at ease?"
"23216","(23216) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid bin Dinar, on the authority of Amer: Concerning a man who lends a loan to another. And he intends to perform a better decree than that. He said: That is more wicked."
"23217","(23217) Waki’ told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: A man borrowed dirhams from Ibn Masoud. So he fulfilled it, and the man said to him: I have overpaid you for my generous giving. Ibn Masoud disliked that and said: like my coins."
"23218","(23218) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Hisham al-Dastawai narrated to us, on the authority of al-Qasim bin Abi Bazza, on the authority of Ata bin Yaqoub, He said: Ibn Umar borrowed a thousand dirhams from me, and he repaid me his dirhams, which were better than his own. He said: There was no bounty in them, so he Something from me to you, will you accept it? I said: Yes."
"23219","(23219) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shuabi, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about a man who lends dirhams to a man and is given them. Better than that? They said: There is no problem as long as his intention was not that."
"23220","(23220) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: Zakaria bin Abi Zaydā narrated to us, on the authority of Amir, who said: I asked him about the man who lends money. If a man buys dirhams and is given something better? He said: There is no problem as long as he did not do it intentionally or as a condition."
"23221","(23221) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, saying: I heard a sheikh called: Al-Mughirah, he said: I said to Ibn Omar: I lend advances to my neighbors and they give me better dirhams than mine. He said: There is no problem as long as you do not stipulate."
"23222","(23222) Ismail bin Ayyash narrated to us, on the authority of Salma bin Alqami, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Whoever buys a garment with a condition So he sold it for a profit before he was required to buy it, as the profit goes to the owner of the garment."
"23223","(23223) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: Whoever buys something with a condition and sells it before It is necessary for it, and whatever virtue it contains, it is for the first."
"23224","(23224) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Zam’i, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, he said: If he buys, sells it on the condition that He had a choice, so he sold it before its owner came, so it was permissible to sell it and it was permissible for him."
"23225","(23225) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Mutarrif ibn Utba, on the authority of his father, who was a friend of Shuraih, who said: I said to Shurayh: I will go to the market and buy the dress and stipulate that there is a choice in it, then I will go. If I sell it, I will take the profit. Otherwise I will reject him. He said: Do not do it."
"23226","(23226) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Sa’id bin Zayd bin Uqba, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Samra, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever loses his belongings, or has his belongings stolen and finds them in the hands of a man, I have more right to it, and the buyer returns to the seller. (Ahmad 5/18. Daraqutni 29)"
"23227","(23227) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Hajjar ibn Abjar, on the authority of Ali: Concerning a man who was in He had a garment in his hand, so a man stood over him and said to Ali: Give this his garment, and follow the one from whom you bought it."
"23228","(23228) Ibn Aliya narrated to us, on the authority of Salama bin Alqamiya, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: The judge used to decide whom. He sold something that did not belong to him, so it belongs to its owner. If he asks for it, he will take it for free."
"23229","(23229) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi: The people were partners in the house, so some of them bought from Some said: Others have no intercession."
"23230","(23230) Hafs told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, a similar story."
"23231","(23231) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: A man and I bought a house, and one man gets a sixth and the other gets a sixth. Half, so he sold it to my friend, meaning I will take it all together, or I will take it instead of them. He said: No, rather you will take it instead of them."
"23232","(23232) Al-Dahhak ibn Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Ibn Abi Husayn informed me, on the authority of a peacock who said: It is in it. Either way"
"23233","(23233) Abdullah bin Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Thabit, who said: I heard Ata’ narrate that a man pawned a horse with a man. So he paid in his possession, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to the mortgager: Your right is gone.\n(Abu Dawud 1888, Bayhaqi 41)"
"23234","(23234) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, who said: I heard a commentator saying: The bet is gone with what is in it."
"23235","(23235) Ali bin Mushar told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: Betting on what is in it."
"23236","(23236) Ibn Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: The bet is gone with what is in it."
"23237","(23237) Ibn Abi Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Shurayh, similar to this."
"23238","(23238) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Betting on what is in it."
"23239","(23239) Ibn Aliya told us, he said: I asked Ibn Abi Najih about a mortgage if he dies. He said: Ata used to say: Gold, silver, and precious metals come back and forth, but animals do not come back and forth. He is among the first."
"23240","(23240) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If the bet is for more than what he bet for, He is trustworthy in giving good deeds, but if he is deficient, it is better for him to have the deficiency restored to him."
"23241","(23241) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Zam’i, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: The bet is of what is in it."
"23242","(23242) Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin, who said: The bet is on what is in it."
"23243","(23243) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Idris al-Awdi narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Umayrah, he said: I heard Ibn Umar saying in Al-Rahn: They seek credit."
"23244","(23244) Waki’ narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ali, he said: They seek credit in The mortgage"
"23245","(23245) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Saleh, on the authority of Abd al-A’la bin Amir, on the authority of Muhammad bin al-Hanafiyyah, on the authority of Ali He said: If the bet is more than what he bet on, then it is destroyed, then it is due for what is in it, because he is trustworthy in giving credit, and if it is Less than what he bet with, and it is lost, and the bettor returns the credit."
"23246","(23246) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Qaqa’ bin Yazid, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: If the mortgage More than what he bet for, then he is destroyed, so he is rewarded with what is in it, because he is trustworthy in virtue, and if it is less than what he bet for So he perished, the mortgager returned the credit."
"23247","(23247) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Shabak, he said: I said to Ibrahim: A man took a bet."
"23248","(23248) Waki’ told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Amir, who said: Betting on what is in it."
"23249","(23249) Waki’ told us, he said: Shu’ba told us, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Sharih, he said: The bet is on what is in it. Shu’ba said: I said to the ruling regarding his statement: If it is less or more, is it equal? He said: Yes."
"23250","(23250) Waki’ told us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, he said: The Messenger of God said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: The mortgage is not closed. It belongs to the one who mortgaged it. He has his sheep and he has his debt.\n(Abdul Razzaq 15033. Ibn Hibban 5934)"
"23251","(23251) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Amir bin Masoud al-Jumahi, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Abdullah bin Jaafar, that a man mortgaged a house for a term, and when the term came, the mortgager said: My house, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: The mortgage shall not be closed."
"23252","(23252) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: We still hear that the mortgage is based on what is in it."
"23253","(23253) Abu Asim told us, on the authority of Imran al-Qattan, on the authority of Matar, on the authority of Ata’, he said: We still hear that the bet is for what is in it."
"23254","(23254) Abu Asim told us, on the authority of Imran al-Qattan, on the authority of Matar, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, on the authority of Omar, he said: If If the bettor is more than what he bet with, then he is trustworthy in the credit, and if it is less then it will be returned."
"23255","(23255) Abdul-Wahhab bin Ata’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, who said: Betting on what is in it."
"23256","(23256) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Jaban, who said: I disputed with Shurayh about a gold ring, and he said: The bet is for what Therein"
"23257","Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Yunus told us, he said: Abu Abdul Rahman Baqi bin Mukhlid told us, he said: Abu Bakr bin told us Abi Shaybah said:\n(23257) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Hassan, on the authority of his mother, Fatima, son of Husayn, that Zayd ibn Harithha came from one of his tribes and needed help from Zahir, so he sold some of them. When he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, saw one of your women crying. He said: What is the matter with this woman? He was informed that Zaid had sold her son, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Return him or buy him."
"23258","(23258) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ali, who said: He was sent with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted me with two captive slave boys whom I sold. When I came to him, he said: Have you gathered or dispersed? I said: I dispersed. He said: Then I will catch up with you. I will catch up with you. (Tirmidhi 1284 and Abu Dawud 2689)"
"23259","(23259) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Farrukh, who said: Omar wrote: Do not differentiate between The two brothers"
"23260","(23260) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Farukh - and he may have said: on the authority of his father: that Omar, he said: Do not differentiate between a mother and her two children."
"23261","(23261) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal, who said: Iqal - or Hakim bin Iqal - said: Othman bin Affan wrote to Iqal: To buy a hundred members of the family and take them to Medina, and do not buy for me. Something that will separate him from his parents."
"23262","(23262) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Habib ibn Shihab, on the authority of his father: He fought with Abu Musa, but when they conquered there was no cover. It differentiates between the woman and her children in the sale."
"23263","(23263) Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Musa ibn Ali, who said: I heard Ibn Abi Jabali al-Qurashi saying: They were They disperse the captives, then Abu Ayyub comes and gathers them together."
"23264","(23264) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They only disliked selling slaves for fear that they would separate The child, his father, and his brothers."
"23265","(23265) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Masoud said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought captives, he would give all of the Ahl al-Bayt permission to do so. He separates them. (Ibn Majah 2248. Ahmad 389)"
"23266","(23266) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal, on the authority of Hakim bin Aqal, who said: Othman wrote to my father to buy for me a hundred household members and do not separate a father from his children."
"23267","(23267) Ishaq Al-Azraq narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Muhammad: They both hated to be separated between The mother and her children."
"23268","(23268) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan: He hated it, and he said: There is no harm in it if it is described, or I was described."
"23269","(23269) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Ismail, on the authority of Taliq bin Imran, on the authority of Abu Burda, on the authority of Abu Moses: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the separation between a mother and her children in the sale. (Ibn Majah 2250, Darqutni 254)"
"23270","(23270) Saal bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: I wrote to Nafi’ asking him about the Ahl al-Bayt. They are the man's. Is it appropriate for him to separate them? He said: He said: I do not know that that is forbidden, but it is disliked by her."
"23271","(23271) Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of Dawud ibn Abi al-Qassaf, on the authority of Riyah ibn Ubaidah: Omar bin Abdulaziz wrote to him to sell one of the slaves of the Emirate and to sell the people of The whole house, and there is no distinction between them."
"23272","(23272) Ibn Abi Zaydi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Amir, who said: Omar wrote: Do you not separate between the captives? And their children."
"23273","(23273) Ibn Abi Zaydah narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid Ibn Ibrahim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: I was informed that a son of a son Omar said to him: Do you hate to separate the mother from her son when you have separated me from my mother?!"
"23274","(23274) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, raised by him, who said: Whenever the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came Upon him being taken captive, he gave him Ahl al-Bayt: Ahl al-Bayt, but he did not like to be separated among them."
"23275","(23275) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim: He sold the daughter of his maidservant, he said Mansour: So I said to him: Did they not hate separation? He said: Yes! But her mother was satisfied and I placed her in a suitable place."
"23276","(23276) Waki’ told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer, Ata’, and Muhammad bin Ali, they said: There is no harm in Differentiate between generators."
"23277","(23277) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no harm in him if he or she is described.\n Waki` said: There should be no distinction between captives, but as for the women giving birth, if they do not need their mothers, then there is no problem."
"23278","(23278) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir and Abu Jafar: They disliked the separation between the captives, so as for the newborns, It's okay"
"23279","(23279) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Amer, who said: Abdullah said: You have not committed any error in Islam, meaning, there is no mistake."
"23280","(23280) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin: He did not allow error."
"23281","(23281) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer: Concerning a man who sold a garment to another man and said: I made a mistake, so he said: Al-Shaabi: It is nothing, the sale is a deception, and Al-Qasim said: He will return it."
"23282","(23282) Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah, the client of Amr bin Harith, narrated to us, on the authority of his father, who said: A man from the people of He set out with ten camels, so he gave him one hundred and thirty for the camels, and one hundred and twenty, but he refused, so he came to him. A man from the slavers said: I took it from you for a thousand lots, so he sold it, but when he calculated it, he regretted it! So he disputed with him to Shurayh, so he approved the sale and said: The sale is a deception."
"23283","(23283) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade selling food. Until he completes the two saa’s, then he will have an increase and a decrease for him. (Ibn Majah 2228. Daraqutni 24)"
"23284","(23284) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Ubaidah, who said: It is forbidden to sell food until it is sold. The two saa’s, the increase is for the one who bought, and the decrease is for the seller."
"23285","(23285) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin and Al-Hasan: They were asked about the man who buys Should I sell food for a kilogram? They said: No, until he completes the two saa’s in it, and he will have the increase and he will have the decrease."
"23286","(23286) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi and Al-Hakam: Concerning a man who buys food and adds more. They said: If it was wrong, return it, and if it was extra, return it."
"23287","(23287) Affan told us, he said: Mahdi bin Maymun told us, on the authority of Asim bin Bashir bin Al-Bara’, he said: I heard Muwarriq Al-Ijlili says: We have sent a ship from Al-Awaz to Basra containing thirty kurs, which is nothing but the surplus between them. Alkylene"
"23288","(23288) Omar told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If you sell food and find an increase, you have it, or a decrease, you must do so."
"23289","(23289) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Ali, who said: If he acknowledges himself with servitude, then Abd"
"23290","(23290) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: No free man can be enslaved. By admitting himself to slavery."
"23291","(23291) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Al-Harith: Concerning a man who says: I was owned by so-and-so, or he was my father. Owned by so-and-so, or was my mother owned by so-and-so, and so-and-so said: You are my slaves today. He said: If they were Concerning emancipation, and it is known that they are loyal, they will not be for this purpose the ones they call upon, unless he brings just witnesses. They bear witness that they are kings to this day."
"23292","(23292) Yahya bin Zakariya bin Abi Zaydi told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Ghaniyya, on the authority of the ruling, he said: If he joins One of the negotiators is a debtor, so he owes them both."
"23293","(23293) Ibn Abi Za’idah told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: The guarantor is in debt."
"23294","(23294) Ibn Abi Zaydah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: I said to Shurayh: My guarantor is my guarantor. And my property was appointed in my name, and the property of my debtor was divided without me. He said: If the guarantor has the choice, then the guarantor is a debtor, even if he If your property is claimed, then you have more right to it, and if your debtor’s property is divided instead of you, then it is in shares."
"23295","(23295) Ismail bin Ayyash narrated to us, on the authority of Sharhabeel bin Muslim, who said: I heard Abu Imamah Al-Bayli saying: I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in his sermon in the year of the Farewell Hajj, said: The debt is repaid and the leader is in debt. Meaning: the guarantor."
"23296","(23296) Ismail Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid and Tawoos: In the Almighty’s saying: {Then write to them if you know of any good in them.} They said: Wealth and trusts."
"23297","(23297) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, about Ata’: his performance and his money."
"23298","(23298) Ibn Abi Zayedah and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Ubaidah, who said: If he prays."
"23299","(23299) Ibn Abi Zayedah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: His best: his performance and his money."
"23300","(23300) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: When he prays."
"23301","(23301) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan: {Then write them down if you know any good in them} He said: Religion and trust."
"23302","(23302) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Abi Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Salih, saying: Performance and security."
"23303","(23303) Waki’ told us, he said: Shu’ba told us, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: Money."
"23304","(23304) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan and Malik bin Mughul narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Truthfully Loyalty"
"23305","(23305) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Malik bin Mughul narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’, he said: Money."
"23306","(23306) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Ibn Abbas said: {If you knew about them... Good} Ibn Abbas said: Good: money."
"23307","(23307) Shababah narrated to us, on the authority of Warqa’, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid: {Then write to them if you know of them. Good} He said: Their morals are whatever they are."
"23308","(23308) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan: In the Almighty’s saying: {So write them. Did you know good about them? He said: Good: the Qur’an and Islam.\n Saeed bin Abi Al-Hassan said: Islam and wealth."
"23309","(23309) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaidah bin Abi Salih, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: Who is responsible for A man who is guaranteed something, and he did not command him to do it and he paid it on his behalf. The person being paid for has nothing, it is only a burden. Bear with it."
"23310","(23310) Hafs told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Zaid, on the authority of Talha bin Abdullah bin Awf, who said: The command of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He greeted a caller and called out until he came to the second: Verily, the witness of an adversary, nor of those who suspect, is not permissible, and the oath is upon the one who claims. Aliyah"
"23311","(23311) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: I will refute six witnesses: the adversary. And the suspicious person, and the one who pays the debt, and the partner to his partner, and the hired worker to the one who hires him, and the slave to his master."
"23312","(23312) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It is not permissible in divorce to be witnesses of two suspects, nor one who is accused."
"23313","(23313) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Shurayh said: I do not accept the testimony of an opponent or a doubtful person. Nor one who pays a debt, nor a partner to his partner, nor an employee to one who hires him, nor a slave to his master."
"23314","(23314) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Shuraih, he said: It is not permissible for a son to bear witness. Nor a father to his son, nor a wife to her husband, nor a husband to his wife."
"23315","(23315) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: It is not permissible for the father to testify. To his child, nor the child to his father, nor the wife to her husband, nor the husband to his wife, nor the slave to his master, nor the master For his servant, nor for a partner for his partner, nor for each one of them for its owner."
"23316","(23316) Ibn Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Amir: He did not allow a man to testify to his father. A woman does not bear witness to her husband, but it is permissible for a man to bear witness to his son, and a man to bear witness to his wife."
"23317","(23317) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Ansari told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan: He used to say: It is not permissible to be a witness. A man is to his son, nor is a son’s testimony to his father, nor is a husband’s testimony to his wife, nor is a wife’s testimony to her husband."
"23318","(23318) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Shabib bin Gharqadī, who said: I witnessed a narrator who approved of his testimony. A husband to his wife, and it was said to him: He is a husband, and he said: And who can bear witness to a woman except her husband?"
"23319","(23319) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Layla used to permit the husband’s testimony to his wife, but he did not permit The woman’s testimony to her husband."
"23320","(23320) Abu Nu’aym told us, on the authority of Abu Janab, on the authority of Aoun, on the authority of Shuraih: He permitted the witnesses of a father and a husband."
"23321","(23321) Shababi told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Suleiman bin Abi Suleiman, he said: I testified for my father at Abi Bakr bin Hazm approved your testimony."
"23322","(23322) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Maimun, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz: He permitted Magi witness against a Jew or a Christian."
"23323","(23323) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Yahya bin Wathhab, on the authority of Shurayh: He used to approve the testimony of the People of the Book over others."
"23324","(23324) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Issa bin Abi Izzah, on the authority of Amir: He approved a witness. A Jew over a Christian, or a Christian over a Jew."
"23325","(23325) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Khaled bin Abdul Rahman bin Bukayr Al-Sulami narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: I witnessed a story in which the witnesses of a people of polytheism approved of one another, with their socks soaked."
"23326","(23326) Zayd bin Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Aoun bin Muammar, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Sayegh, he said: I asked Nafi’ about his testimony. The People of the Book were against one another, and He said: It is permissible."
"23327","(23327) Waki` told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, he said: Did you ask Hammad? He said: It is permissible for all polytheists to bear witness against one another."
"23328","(23328) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan said: Islam is a sect and polytheism is a sect, it is permissible for one to bear witness against the other.\n He said: And Waki` said: And so we say."
"23329","(23329) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan: He used to say: If the sects differ, it is not permissible to be a witness. each other against each other."
"23330","(23330) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, who said: It is not permissible for a Jew to testify against a Christian, nor The Christian is over the Jew, and there is no religion over another religion except the Muslims."
"23331","(23331) Waki’ narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: It is not permissible for a sect to bear witness against a sect except Muslims"
"23332","(23332) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri and Hammad, who said: It is not permissible for the People of the Book to bear witness against one another. Some"
"23333","(23333) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It is not permissible to testify to the People of the Book. each other against each other."
"23334","(23334) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, Al-Shu’biy and Al-Hasan. They said: It is not permissible to bear witness. The people of a sect, except for the people of its sect: the Jew against the Jew, and the Christian against the Christian."
"23335","(23335) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak: He did not accept the testimony of the mullahs of Ali. Other than them"
"23336","(23336) Wakī’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bā, he said: I asked the arbiter about the testimony of a Jew against a Christian. And the Christian over the Jew? He said: The ruling: It is not permissible for people of a religion to bear witness against other people."
"23337","(23337) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Omar bin Rashid narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abi Salma bin Abdul Rahman said: It is not permissible for a sect to bear witness to a sect except Muslims.\n Waki` said: Ibn Abi Layla did not allow a Jew to testify against a Christian, nor did a Christian testify against a Christian. The Jew\n(Abdul Razzaq 15525. Bayhaqi 163)"
"23338","(23338) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Jahm, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It is permissible for the People of the Book to bear witness to one another. On some for Muslims."
"23339","(23339) Asbat bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: It is permissible for Muslims to testify against one another. Some"
"23340","(23340) Sharik told us, on the authority of Abbas, on the authority of Shurayh. On the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer, they said: There is no guarantee for the slave."
"23341","(23341) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Qatadah and Hamid, on the authority of Al-Hasan: A man from Quraysh stole A camel, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, cut off his hand. He said: His testimony was permissible. (Abu Dawud 395)"
"23342","(23342) Ibn Abi Zaydi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: He testified at Shurayh’s place that I was cutting, so he praised me. May goodness be upon him. Shurayh said: We will reward the witness of the one who bears every punishment when there is a just witness on the day, except for the slanderer, then his repentance is between them. And God made it clear."
"23343","(23343) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Shurayh: He permitted a witness to be cut off."
"23344","(23344) Ibn Abi Za’idah and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Amir, who said: Ali was brought about some matter, and he said: Waki`: Concerning something, and he said: It is unjust, and had it not been for the sake of peace, I would have rejected it."
"23345","(23345) Ibn Abi Zaydi told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: Whatever woman is reconciled to An eighth of it, and it was not explained to her what her husband left, so that is the entire interest."
"23346","(23346) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: I have never seen anyone who ordered reconciliation except that he passed by it. This is because a black man entrusted a woman with eighty dirhams, but she transferred her belongings, and the dirhams were lost, so he disputed with her to a point. He said: Did you orphan her? He said: No, he said: If you wish, you can take fifty."
"23347","(23347) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Abdullah bin Utba: He may have come to him. The people dispute with him about something, and he says: Go and make peace."
"23348","(23348) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ash-Shu’bi, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, that he said: Perhaps he came to slander the people. They dispute with him, and he says: Go to my servants."
"23349","(23349) Waki’ told us, he said: Mis’ar told us, on the authority of Azhar Al-Attar, on the authority of Muharib bin Dathar, Omar said: Repel the adversaries. Until they reconcile, because the severance of justice creates grudges among the people."
"23350","(23350) Waki’ told us, he said: Jarir bin Hazim told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: Omar bin Al-Khattab sent a judge, Then two men disputed with him over a dinar. He said: So he gave one of them to him, and he gave the other a dinar from him, and that age reached the age of So he sent for him and he isolated him."
"23351","(23351) Abdullah bin Mubarak told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: If the two opponents are satisfied with the statement of a man, then it is permissible for them both. What he said"
"23352","(23352) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Asim al-Ahwal, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: Two men came They disputed with his servants, and he said: Do you appoint me as a leader over you? They said: Yes, so he decided between them."
"23353","(23353) Abdul Salam narrated to us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah, meaning Ibn Abi Farwa, on the authority of Ghaylan, who said: I said to Omar bin Abdul Aziz: If you change these dirhams, they will fall into the hands of the Jew, the Christian, the foreigner, and the Magi. He said: You want the nations to protest against us, you want us to change the monotheism of our Lord and the name of our Prophet?!"
"23354","(23354) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Fada’, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Alqamah bin Abdullah, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade breaking the permissible peg of Muslims among them, except for those who are valiant.\n(Abu Dawud 3443. Hakim 31)"
"23355","(23355) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The people sinned when they struck white dirhams."
"23356","(23356) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abu Farwa, he heard Ibn Abi Layla, he said: Omar bin Al-Khattab said: Who Its leaf has become dead, so let him not swear to people that it is good, but if he goes out with it to the market, let him say: Who will sell it to me? With these false dirhams, he crushed a garment or an item he needed."
"23357","(23357) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of his father, on the authority of a man from among the fat people, who said: Ali said: If it was for one of you Dirhams that cannot be spent on his behalf, let him buy gold with them, and let him buy with the gold what he can spend on his behalf."
"23358","(23358) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Salma bin Nubait narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Dahhak bin Muzahim, who said: Ibn Masoud sold his exile. He went to the treasury once, then he met Omar and did not do that again."
"23359","(23359) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim: Omar prohibited Abdullah from selling the waste of a house. Money"
"23360","(23360) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Misra, on the authority of Hawt al-Abdi, who said: Abdullah placed me in charge of the treasury, so if a false dirham passed by me I would break it."
"23361","(23361) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Maymun ibn Abi Shabib: that when a false dirham passed by him, he would break it. And he says: Muslims will not be deceived by it."
"23362","(23362) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Aoun narrated to us, saying: I said to Muhammad bin Sirin: I buy with counterfeit dirhams. And make it clear? He said: No problem."
"23363","(23363) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Abu Ja`far al-Razi narrated to us, on the authority of al-Rabi’ ibn Anas, he said: I saw Safwan ibn Mahrez He came to the market with a fake dirham and said: Who will sell me good grapes for an evil dirham?! So he bought and did not testify."
"23364","(23364) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Rabi’ narrated to us, saying: I said to Al-Hasan: O Abu Sa’id, I have coins and copper. Shall I sell it and show it? He said: No problem."
"23365","(23365) Ziyad bin Al-Rabi’ narrated to us, on the authority of Salih Al-Dahhan, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid: That when it fell into his hands He broke a fake dirham and said: It is not permissible for a Muslim to be deceived with it."
"23366","(23366) Muhammad bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Qays: That Saeed bin Jubayr had a dirham in his hand, So I said to him: Show me it, and he gave it to me, and said: If it had been bad, I would not have given it to you."
"23367","(23367) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri: That Muadh bin Jabal fell into debt. So the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave him some of his money to his creditors."
"23368","(23368) Waki’ told us, he said: Hassan bin Salih told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Shuraih, he said: He used to sell what is above The loincloth"
"23369","(23369) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Umar ibn Abdul Rahman ibn Dalaf, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his uncle His father, Bilal bin Al-Harith, said: He was a man who exaggerated in camels, and preceded the pilgrims, until he went bankrupt. He said: Then he proposed to Omar bin Al-Khattab said: As for what follows, the most generous reward for Jihan is his satisfaction with his trustworthiness and his religion. It is said: He preceded the Hajj and performed it. He refused, and in the morning he owed it, so whoever owes him anything, let him come to us so that we may divide his money among them. (Malik 8)"
"23370","(23370) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib: that Omar bin Abdul Aziz did not sell A servant of man, and his abode is not in religion."
"23371","(23371) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Maimun, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz: He was a bankrupt man. And he rewarded him."
"23372","(23372) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Shurayh: That when he went bankrupt A man who made what was left between his fines."
"23373","(23373) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is nothing wrong with it."
"23374","(23374) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Salem, Al-Qasim, Tawus, Mujahid, and Muhammad bin Ali. And Ataa, they said: There is no harm in offering peace in silk.\n He said: Waki` said: We hope that there will be no harm in him."
"23375","(23375) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Fazza’ ibn Afiq, who said: I said to Ibn Umar: What do you say about theft? He said: What is theft? I said: Silk, or slits of silk. He said: O people of Iraq, you are called objectionable names. Didn’t you say: slits of silk? ?! I said: It has a price in the market and we buy it for that price, and we sell it to the giver for more than that. He said: If you buy it And you took possession of it, sell it as you wish."
"23376","(23376) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Abdullah bin Al-Walid Al-Muzani narrated to us, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ibn Maqil: He hated peace. In silk."
"23377","(23377) Mu`tamir narrated to us, on the authority of his father, he said: Tawus was asked about peace in the width, or he said: the widths, he said: There is no problem. He was asked about peace in silk? He said: I do not know what silk is."
"23378","(23378) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Israel and Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Masruq: He disliked peace in Silk"
"23379","(23379) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir: He disliked peace in silk."
"23380","(23380) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’biyy. On the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, they said: Whatever is taken away from the mortgage, it is on account of that."
"23381","(23381) Yahya bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: I asked him about a man who rented a house and it burned down. He said: His right is what is gone, and his right is what remains."
"23382","(23382) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salamah, on the authority of his followers: Concerning a man who mortgaged a house and it burned down. He said: His right is in The throne"
"23383","(23383) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim: Concerning a man who pawned a garment. So he relied and said: He will throw from it the same amount as the value of the garment was reduced."
"23384","(23384) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: If the mortgagee takes possession of the mortgage, and then he dies The bettor has a debt, so he is more deserving of it than the debtors until it is repaid."
"23385","(23385) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Ata’, Salim, and Aamir. They said: If the bettor dies and it is upon him. A debt. The mortgager has more right to it than the debtors until it is paid."
"23386","(23386) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of the ruling: Concerning a man who bets a mortgage, then If its owner dies, leaving no money other than the mortgage, and does he have a debt equal to that of the mortgage holder? He said: The mortgagee has more right to the mortgage than the fines of the dead person."
"23387","(23387) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: A mortgage taken if its owner dies or becomes bankrupt. The one in his hand has more right to it. If it is not taken, then he is among the creditors."
"23388","(23388) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Zakaria narrated to us, Amer narrated to us: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, granted permission to witness. Khuzaymah bin Thabit with the testimony of two men. (Abu Dawud 3602. An-Nasa’i 6243)"
"23389","(23389) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Imran bin Hudayr narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Majliz, he said: I witnessed Zurara bin He fulfilled my testimony alone, so he accepted my testimony, and wretched is what he did."
"23390","(23390) Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I bore witness with Shurayh as my only witness upon my will. He approved your testimony."
"23391","(23391) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: Shurayh said to me: You bear witness that it was your handwriting. In your hand, and my hope is upon you? I said: Yes, so he allowed my testimony alone."
"23392","(23392) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Qais: that Shurayh permitted his testimony alone on the Qur’an."
"23393","(23393) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Shurayh: He approved his testimony alone."
"23394","(23394) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Ibn Maqil: Concerning a man who owes a debtor to another man and he denies it. Then he gives him money? He said: He will not oppose it, he will fulfill your trust."
"23395","(23395) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: He is Asaad."
"23396","(23396) Abd al-Salam narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’. He said: A man of our companions had money over a man, but he denied it, then it came to him. Something, and he came to me and asked me and our companions, and they said: Should he take it? And I asked Ibn Maqil? He said: He fulfills his trust and asks for his rights. If he has something between you, he will fulfill his rights, otherwise he will swear to him."
"23397","(23397) Abd al-Salam told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin: That when he was asked about this, he would recite this. Verse: {And if you punish, then punish with the like of what you were punished with}"
"23398","(23398) Abd al-Salam told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He takes possession unless he swears an oath."
"23399","(23399) Waki’ told us, he said: Shu’abi told us, he said: I asked the ruling about a man who has a debt over a debtor. So he denies him, and then the money falls to him? Al-Hakam said: Abraham said: There is no harm in taking the oath as long as he does not fear that he will be asked to take an oath.\n He said: Waki` said: Thus we say."
"23400","(23400) Waki’ told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of his father, he said: It is written in the Torah: Do not betray a traitor. His betrayal is enough for you."
"23401","(23401) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Miskin Abu Hurairah al-Taymi narrated to us, saying: I asked Mujahid about that? He said: Do not betray him."
"23402","(23402) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Shu`ba narrated to us, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Do not betray him."
"23403","(23403) Khalid bin Al-Harith narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Makin: that Abu Majlaz and Yahya bin Aqeel, one of them said: A man betrayed me and went away with a dirham, and now he has a dirham. Should I not take from his dirhams as he took from his? ? He said to me: You do not take it so that I will not take it. The other said: But I will take it."
"23404","(23404) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Rabi’ told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Return the trusts. And do not betray those who betray you. (Bukhari 3142, Abu Dawud 3529)"
"23405","(23405) Waki` narrated to us, saying: I heard Sufyan saying: There is no harm in separating gold from gold, and silver from gold. Silver, and he does not cut off any gold or silver items.\n He said: Waki` said: And so we say."
"23406","(23406) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: He is the happiest with him."
"23407","(23407) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If a servant becomes bankrupt and acknowledges the debt, then it is not permissible His saying"
"23408","(23408) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Hikam, who said: The debt of the slave is not paid except With what we have shown."
"23409","(23409) Yazeed bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Salim, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: It is not permissible for a property to acknowledge a debt except To be authorized to trade."
"23410","(23410) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: He hated to say: I will direct you to the goods and you will share them with me."
"23411","(23411) Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi told us, on the authority of Abu Hurriya, on the authority of al-Hasan: Concerning a man who said: I will guide you to the sale of such-and-such. And such and such, and do you include my brother in it? He said: Selling by mutual consent."
"23412","(23412) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi: He disliked letting a man guide him. On the provision that He should associate with Him."
"23413","(23413) Jarir told us, on the authority of Qaboos, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in the Almighty’s saying: {O you who have believed, be They are guardians of justice.} He said: The two men sit with the judge, so the judge has the power and coercion of one of the two men rather than The other"
"23414","(23414) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Al-Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: There is no An arbitrator who rules between the people, but he will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection, and an angel will take his scruff until he stands with it over Hell, then he will be raised. His head to the Most Gracious, and if he says to him: Throw it away, then he will cast it into the abode of forty sheep.\n He said: And Masruq said: Because a day spent in justice and justice is more beloved to me than a Sunnah that I fight for the sake of God.\n(Ibn Majah 2311. Ahmad 1/430)"
"23415","(23415) Abu Muawiyah told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Al-Manhal, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: The affliction of Solomon that afflicted him was among some of the people of the locusts, and the locust was a woman, and he was Solomon intended that the truth be for the people of the locusts, so he would judge for them accordingly. (Nasa’i 10993. Tabari 449)"
"23416","(23416) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sa`id bin Abdul Aziz al-Tanukhi narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Ubaid Allah bin Abi Al-Muhajir, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanam al-Ash`ari, said: Omar said: Woe to the judge of the people of the earth from the judge of the people of the heavens. On the Day they will meet him, except one who has maintained justice and decided according to truth, and he has not fulfilled his desire, nor kinship, nor out of his own desire, nor out of desire. To his terror, and He made the Book of God a mirror between his eyes."
"23417","(23417) Shabab bin Siwar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of his leaders, he said: I heard a report raised by Aba Al-Aliyah, he said: He said: Ali: The judges are three: two in Hell, and one in Paradise. So he mentioned those who are in Hell. He said: A man who is unjust intentionally. So this person will be in Hell, and a man who wanted the truth and made a mistake is in Hell, and another man who wanted the truth and made a mistake and is in Paradise. He said: So I said to Rafi’: Have you seen this one who wanted the truth but made a mistake? He said: If the judge did not know, his right was not to be a judge.\n(Tirmidhi 1322 and Abu Dawud 3568)"
"23418","(23418) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah informed us, on the authority of his leaders: that Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, said: It is not appropriate for a judge to make a ruling until the truth becomes clear to him just as the night is distinguished from the day. He said: So that was the case. Omar said: Abu Musa spoke the truth."
"23419","(23419) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan: In his statement (and Fasl Al-Khattab), he said: Knowledge of judgment."
"23420","(23420) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: Witnesses and faith."
"23421","(23421) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid: In his saying: (He gives wisdom to whom He wills) he said: It is not Prophecy, but it is science, the Qur’an, and jurisprudence."
"23422","(23422) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ziyad, who said: (Fasl Al-Khattab), as for what follows."
"23423","(23423) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: Witnesses and faith."
"23424","(23424) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Bakra, on the authority of his father, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The arbitrator does not rule between two people while he is angry."
"23425","(23425) Zayd ibn Harun told us, he said: Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shurayh, he said: What I have never witnessed the whims of an opponent, nor have I ever taught him his proof."
"23426","(23426) Ubaidah narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakra, on the authority of his father, He said: The arbitrator does not judge between two people while they are angry. (Bukhari 7158 and Muslim 1342)"
"23427","(23427) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Hisham bin Urwah narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Zainab bint Umm Salamah, on the authority of Umm She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: You dispute with me, but I am only human, and perhaps some of you He will be more consistent with his argument than some of them, but I will only judge between you according to what I hear from you, so whoever I have judged is worthy of justice. I tell my brother something, but he will not take it. Rather, I will cut off for him a piece of the Fire, which he will bring on the Day of Resurrection. (Bukhari 6967 and Muslim 1337)"
"23428","(23428) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Usama bin Zaid al-Laythi narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Rafi’, the client of Umm Salama, On the authority of Umm Salamah, she said: Two men from the Ansar came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to dispute the inheritances between them. I have studied the differences between you, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: You are disputing before me, but I am only a human being. Perhaps some of you will be more eloquent in their argument than others, but I will only judge between you according to what I hear from you. I have fulfilled for him something that is due to his brother, but he will not take it, but I will allocate for him a piece of Hell for him, and he will bring it. He would be stabbed in the neck on the Day of Resurrection. She said: Then the two men cried and each of them said: Defend my brother. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: As for when you both do that, go and divide them and strive for the truth, then ask each other for advice, then let each one of you make it permissible. His companion\n(Abu Dawud 3579. Daraqutni 123)"
"23429","(23429) Muhammad ibn Bishr al-Abdi narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, saying: Abu Salama narrated to us, on the authority of my father. Harry, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: I am only human, and perhaps some of you will be melodious with your argument from Some, so whoever has his brother’s rights cut off from him, I only cut off from him a portion of the Fire. (Ahmad 2/332, Ibn Hibban 5071)"
"23430","(23430) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Aoun narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Shurayh: that he used to say to the opponents: The oppressors will know the rights of those who wronged them. The oppressor awaits punishment, and the oppressed awaits victory."
"23431","(23431) Ibn Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: There was a share of what he says to the opponent: O Abdullah By God, I will judge for you, and indeed I think you are unjust, but I will not judge based on suspicion, but I will judge based on what you have brought me, and if A judicial ruling does not make lawful for you what was forbidden to you."
"23432","(23432) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-A’la bin Amir al-Tha’labi, on the authority of Bilal bin Abi Burda. Ibn Abi Musa, on the authority of Anas Ibn Malik, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He who asks for judgment is entrusted to himself. And whoever is forced to do so, an angel descends upon him and redeems him. (Tirmidhi 1323 and Abu Dawud 3573)"
"23433","(23433) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Harith Al-Basri, who said: The Children of Israel used to For a man among them is an ounce of prophecy."
"23434","(23434) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Some of the Medinites narrated to us, on the authority of al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever is appointed to judge, it is as if he was slaughtered without a knife."
"23435","(23435) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mas’ar, on the authority of Abi Husayn, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: Judgments are only coals, so push away the coals. With two sticks about you, meaning witnesses."
"23436","(23436) Waki’ told us, he said: Mis’ar told us, on the authority of Ma’an bin Abdul Rahman, he said: Shurayh used to say To the witnesses: I did not leave you, nor will I prevent you if you get up. Rather, it is for you to decide, and I am on guard against you. So be careful for yourselves."
"23437","(23437) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Furat bin Abi Bahr narrated to us, saying: I heard Al-Sha’bi - and a man said to him: Judge between us according to what God bless you - he said: I am not in my opinion to make up for it."
"23438","(23438) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman, who said: When David was ordered to judge, the matter was cut off. With it, God revealed to him: Ask the clear evidence and make them swear to them."
"23439","(23439) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, who said: Al-Hakam bin Ayyub wrote about a group of people whom he would appoint over The judiciary, and Jabir bin Zaid said: If he had been sent to me, I would have fled."
"23440","(23440) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, he said: When Abd al-Rahman ibn Udhainiya died, Abu Qalab mentioned To judge, he fled until he came to the Levant, and this coincided with the removal of its owner, so he fled until he came to Al-Yamamah, and I met him after that. He said: I did not find anything like a judge except that of a man swimming in a sea, and how many times he may swim until he drowns."
"23441","(23441) Mu’ali bin Mansour narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ja’far, on the authority of Uthman bin Muhammad, on the authority of Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Huraira, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever is appointed a judge among the people will be slaughtered without a knife.\n(Tirmidhi 5925. Abu Dawud 3566)"
"23442","(23442) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Awn, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Amr Al-Thaqafi, on the authority of men from the people of Homs was one of the companions of Muadh, on the authority of Muadh: When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent him, he said to him: How do you make up for it? He said: Judge according to what is in the Book of God. He said: If a matter comes to you that is not in the Book of God, he said: Judge according to the Sunnah of the Messenger of God. He said: If it is not a Sunnah from the Messenger of God? He said: I strive to make up my mind. He said: Praise be to God, who gave success to the Messenger of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Tirmidhi 1327. Ahmad 5/236)"
"23443","(23443) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ubaid Allah Al-Thaqafi, who said: When the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was sent May God bless him and grant him peace, Muadh, to Yemen. He said: O Muadh, what do you decide? He said: I will judge according to the Book of God. He said: So if a matter comes to you that is not in the Book of God? He said: I will judge what his Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ruled. He said: If a matter comes to you that is not in the Book of God and he does not decide for it. Is he a prophet and the righteous did not judge him? He said: I am leading the truth with all my might. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Praise be to God who made the Messenger of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He decides with what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is pleased with."
"23444","(23444) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shurayh: that Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him He wrote to her: If something comes to you in the Book of God, then judge by it, and do not let men divert you from it. If a matter comes to you that is not In the Book of God, then look at the Sunnah of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and judge according to it. If what is not in the Book of God comes There is no Sunnah on it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so see what the people have agreed upon and take it, and if it comes to you then it will come to you. It is not in the Book of God, and there was no Sunnah on it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and no one spoke about it. before you, so choose whichever of the two things you want: If you want to strive hard with your opinion and advance, then advance, and if you want to delay, then delay. I do not see delay as anything but good for you. (Nasa’i 5399)"
"23445","(23445) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Yazeed, he said: Increase the number of One day, Abdullah said: O people, a time has come upon us that we will not finish, and we will not be there. Then, God We have decreed that the matter has reached what you see. So whoever of you is presented with a judgment after today, let him judge according to what is in the Book of God. If it comes It is a matter that is not in the Book of God, so let it be decided according to what His Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, decided. If it comes to a matter that is not It is in the Book of God, and his prophet did not decree it, so let him decide according to what the righteous have decreed, for if a matter comes to him that is not in the Book of God His Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, did not decree it, nor did the righteous decree it, so let him strive according to his opinion, and do not say: I fear and I fear, for what is lawful is clear and what is forbidden is clear, and in between that are doubtful matters, so leave what raises you for what does not. May God bless you"
"23446","(23446) Ibn Abi Zayd told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Zayd, on the authority of Abdullah, Like the hadith of Abu Muawiyah."
"23447","(23447) Ibn Abi Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah, something similar to that. It added to it: If something comes to him that he does not know, let him acknowledge it, and not be ashamed."
"23448","(23448) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Abi Yazid, who said: When Ibn Abbas was asked about the matter, And it was in the Qur’an that he told about it, and if it was not in the Qur’an, then it was about the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. With it, and if not, then on the authority of Abu Bakr and Omar, may God be pleased with them, and if not, then he said in his opinion about it."
"23449","(23449) Zaid bin Al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Saif bin Sulaiman Al-Makki narrated to us, on the authority of Qais bin Saad, on the authority of Amr bin A dinar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, decided with the testimony of a witness and an oath.\n(Muslim 3. Abu Dawud 3603)"
"23450","(23450) Zayd ibn Harun told us, he said: Juwayriyah ibn Asma’ informed us, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Yazid, On the authority of a man, on the authority of a person who stole: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, issued a ruling on the testimony of a right-handed witness. (Tirmidhi 1345. Ibn Majah 2371)"
"23451","(23451) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ja`far ibn Muhammad, on the authority of his father: That the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He judged the testimony of a right and right witness. He said: And Ali, may God be pleased with him, judged it before you."
"23452","(23452) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Khaled bin Abi Karimah, on the authority of Abu Ja`far: That the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace Judgment by the testimony of a witness and an oath in law."
"23453","(23453) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Siwar bin Abdullah, who said: I said to Rabi`ah: Your statement regarding Shahada is a witness. And the oath of the one who has the right? He said: It was found in Saad’s book."
"23454","(23454) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Abu Al-Zinad: that Abd al-Hamid was He made an oath in Kufa with the witness. He said: Some of the people of Kufa disapproved of him, so he wrote to Omar bin Abd al-Aziz, so he wrote to him: to judge by oath with the witness, and a sheikh from their sheikhdom said, or he said: from Their greatest: I witnessed a witness who judged on oath with the witness."
"23455","(23455) Yahya bin Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bai, on the authority of Husayn, who said: Abdullah bin Utba judged me. With the testimony of a witness on the right hand of the one who bears the truth."
"23456","(23456) Affan narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Zaid narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Hamid Al-Ataki: That Yahya bin Omar was He judges according to the testimony of a witness and an oath."
"23457","(23457) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Salem, who said: I heard Al-Sha’bi and he was asked about a judge who ruled unjustly, and he said: Al-Shaabi: As for injustice, I do not say anything about it. He says: It is not appropriate for him to be unjust, but whatever judge has judged, he will come. judge after him, so it is not befitting for him to look into his judgement, and to appoint him as his guardian from that as long as he had assumed responsibility for it."
"23458","(23458) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Rashid, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: A free man should not be sold in bankruptcy. He said: And he wrote With that, Omar bin Abdul Aziz, may God Almighty have mercy on him."
"23459","(23459) Muhammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Ayoub Abi Al-Ala, on the authority of his followers, and Abi Hashim: Concerning a man who made a claim before another man. Money, so he said: Give me a guarantor until I produce my evidence. He said: He does not have that."
"23460","(23460) Ubaid Allah ibn Musa told us, he said: Sufyan informed us, on the authority of Uqba ibn Abi Al-Aizar, he said: I came. Al-Sha'bi met a man over whom I had a right over whom I had no clear evidence. So I said: Take a guarantor from him, but he refused. He took from him a guarantor for me."
"23461","(23461) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Abu Al-Fayd, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Yasar, he said: I heard Abu Al-Darda' bargained with a man, and the man swore not to sell it to him, then he gave it to him after that for that price. Abu Al-Darda' said: I am afraid. Or I hate to make you commit a sin."
"23462","(23462) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus bin Abi Ishaq, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Sa`id bin Wahhab, on the authority of Muadh: He bargained A man made a sale, so he swore not to sell it to him, then he invited him to sell it to him, but he refused to buy from him."
"23463","(23463) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq: that Muadh bargained with a man for something and swore not to sell it to him, so he mentioned something similar to it."
"23464","(23464) Ibn Ali told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: I said to him: A man swears on a thing that he will not sell it, then he sells it. Should I buy it from him? He said: Yes, and remind him of his right hand."
"23465","(23465) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, in a similar vein, saying: This is a sign for the right hand."
"23466","(23466) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Mara bin Sharahil, who said that Suhayb sold He took possession of his home from Othman, and stipulated that it be lived in such-and-such and such-and-such."
"23467","(23467) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Qays al-Asadi narrated to us, on the authority of Aoun bin Abdullah bin Utba: that Tamim Al-Dari sold his house and stipulated that it should be lived in for the rest of his life, and he said: My example is like the mother of Moses, whose son was returned to her and she was given a reward. Her breastfeeding"
"23468","(23468) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer: Two women sold two houses of theirs. They made their residence a condition for their lives. He said: Amer: You will live until you die."
"23469","(23469) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Layla used to perform it with us, and as for others, he used to wear it."
"23470","(23470) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Shabib bin Gharqadiya al-Bariqi, he said: I heard a narration saying: Every Muslim has his own condition."
"23471","(23471) Waki’ and Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Abu Awani narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Abi Al-Sha’tha’i, saying: It occurred A man had a wall between him and his neighbour, so his neighbor disputed with him over a block, but he did not force him to build it, and he said to his neighbour: Go and cover yourself."
"23472","(23472) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Abu Masud, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: A man from among those before you was punished, but nothing good was found for him, except that he was a wealthy man who mingled with people. So He says to His servants: Forgive Him for the one who is in difficulty. Then God Almighty said to His angels: We are more deserving of that than Him. They forgave Him for Him."
"23473","(23473) Yunus bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Abu Ja`far al-Khutmi, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ka’b, on the authority of Abu Qatada, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Whoever makes amends for his adversary, or erases his sins, is In the shadow of the Throne on the Day of Resurrection."
"23474","(23474) Yahya bin Abi Bukair told us, on the authority of Zuhayr bin Muhammad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Abdullah bin Saul bin Hanif: Saul bin Hanif narrated to him, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever helps Struggling in the path of God, or grieving in His hardship, or being humbled in His neck, God will shade him in His shade on the Day when there will be no shade but His shadow"
"23475","(23475) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Raba’i, who said: Uqba said: Bin Amr Lahdhifa: Tell me something you heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He says: Among those before you was a man to whom the angel came to take his soul and said: Have you done good? He said: I do not know him, he said: Look, he said: I do not know him except that I was a man who deceived people in this world and mingled with them, so I was I give relief to the needy, and I spare the well-off, and God admits him to Paradise. Aqaba said: And I heard him say that."
"23476","(23476) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Sha’ithi narrated to us, on the authority of Makhoul, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Take your right to chastity, whether it is sufficient, or whether it is not sufficient. (Ibn Majah 2422)"
"23477","(23477) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Raba’i, on the authority of Abu Ease, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Whoever provides relief to a distressed person, or provides relief for him, God will give him shade. His throne"
"23478","(23478) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Ammar bin Umayr, saying: Two men testified at a corpse of a man on the authority of Something. Al-Amash said: I see him. He said: On a mule. He said: We bear witness that this man bought it from this. One of the witnesses said: I bear witness that he is an immoral person. Shurayh said: How would you know that he is an immoral person? Stand up and there will be no witness to you."
"23479","(23479) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Hassan bin Salih narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ja’d bin Dhakwan, who said: A man approached Shurayh. He said: So he called for a witness, and he said: Where is Rabi’ al-Kuwaifir? So he came to him, and Shurayh said: You acknowledged the Kuifar, so he responded. Your testimony"
"23480","(23480) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us: If two men testified against a man that he divorced his wife, then they retracted Their testimony is that he said: The divorce is valid if he had not consummated the marriage with her. The husband gets back to them for half of the dowry, but if he had consummated the marriage with her then no. Something about them. It means: from friendship."
"23481","(23481) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Uthman al-Batti, on the authority of some of Ibrahim’s companions, on the authority of Ibrahim: Concerning a man who gave permission To his servant, a debt followed him, and the master died while owing a debt. He said: It begins with the debt of the master before the debt of the servant.\n Al-Batti said: I do not like that. He begins with the religion of the servant before the religion of the master, because he freed his neck."
"23482","(23482) Abdullah bin Mubarak told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: My craftsman will come and buy some goods from him. And I will increase its price, and if you wish, you can take it from him without that. Should I sell it to him in full? He said: No. Meaning: profitable."
"23483","(23483) Ibn Abi Zaydah narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: Clutching palm trees means to look at it and turn it over."
"23484","(23484) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Ibn Aoun narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin: Concerning a man who said to another man: If I do not give you your rights To such-and-such and such-and-such and he turned to you, and Shurayh said: If his hand misses his foot, he will be fined."
"23485","(23485) Waki’ told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: A man came to Shurayh and said: I I entrusted this with her, and she went while he was looking. So Sharih said: Your witnesses are that she went and he was looking."
"23486","(23486) Ali narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, he said: I asked Saeed bin Jubayr about the Qur’an, whether it will be accepted in its fulfillment. The groves, the houses, the palm trees, and the trees? He thought that"
"23487","(23487) Ibn Abi Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A man asked him while I was listening: Will he accept? The man: The land contains trees, fruits, and houses? He said: No."
"23488","(23488) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far: He hated facing the heads, and did not see In the villages valiantly."
"23489","(23489) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Muthanna bin Saeed Al-Dab’i narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Bashir bin Ka’b, on the authority of Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Make the road seven cubits long.\n(Bukhari 2473, Muslim 143)"
"23490","(23490) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: When you differ over the path, make it seven cubits long. (Ibn Majah 2339. Ahmad 1/235)"
"23491","(23491) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Mansour bin Dinar, on the authority of Abu Ikrimah Al-Makhzoumi, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: None of you should prevent his neighbor from placing a piece of wood on his wall. (Ahmad 2/447)"
"23492","(23492) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: None of you should prevent his neighbor from placing a piece of wood on his wall.\n He said: Abu Hurairah said: Why do I see you turning away from it, and by God, I will throw it at you between your shoulders?\n(Bukhari 2463. Muslim 136)"
"23493","(23493) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Whoever builds a building, let him support it with his neighbor’s wall. (Ahmad 235. Tabarani 11806)"
"23494","(23494) Waki’ narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Asim bin Abi Al-Najjoud, on the authority of Wa’il bin Rabi’i, he said: Ibn Masoud: False witness has been equated with associating partners with God. Then he recited: {So avoid abomination from idols and avoid false speech}"
"23495","(23495) Muhammad bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan Al-Asfari, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Habib bin Al-Numan Al-Asadi, on the authority of Khurraym bin Fatik said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the morning prayer, and when he left, he stood up and said: The false witness has been judged. By associating others with God three times, then he recited these verses: {And avoid false speech, being true to God, not associating with Him}"
"23496","(23496) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Mas’udi narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim bin Muhammad bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of His father, he said: Omar bin Al-Khattab said: No one in Islam should be held accountable by false witness, for we only accept the just.\n(Malik 720)"
"23497","(23497) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of Ibn al-Hanafiyy: {And do not adopt that of which you have no knowledge} He said: False witness"
"23498","(23498) Abu Bakr and Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Wa’il bin Rabi’a, who said: The false witness is equated with polytheism. By God, and one of them recited: {And those who do not bear witness to falsehood} and the other recited: {And avoid false speech}"
"23499","(23499) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Shu’abi narrated to us, on the authority of Asim bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Aamir bin Rabi’ah. He said: I witnessed Omar ibn Al-Khattab having a false witness stay in a garment for the evening and flaunt himself. (Abdul Razzaq 15388)"
"23500","(23500) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, he said: Shurayh used to send a false witness. To the mosque of his people, or to his market: Indeed, we have falsified this witness."
"23501","(23501) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Mas’udi told us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, he said: Al-Qasim sat with me and said: Whatever it was. Who makes a mark on a false witness when he catches him? He said: I said: He would have his name written down with him, and if he was an Arab, he would send him to his people’s mosque, and if he was an Arab, he would send him to his people’s mosque. The master sent him to his market, informing them of this from him."
"23502","(23502) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ja’d ibn Dhakwan, who said: I witnessed a slew hitting a false witness. With a heartbeat, he removed his turban from his head."
"23503","(23503) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, who said: A people testified with Omar bin Abd. Mighty God, the Crescent of Ramadan, came to them and struck them seventy times, and invalidated their testimony."
"23504","(23504) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: The witness of falsehood will be punished."
"23505","(23505) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: A false witness hits something and identifies people. It is said: This one bore false witness."
"23506","(23506) Abbad narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: A false witness strikes what is less than forty: thirty-five, Thirty-six, thirty-seven."
"23507","(23507) Al-Muharbibi told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Saeed: Omar bin Abdul Aziz flogged the false witness with seventy lashes."
"23508","(23508) Al-Muharbibi narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ja’ad Abu Uthman, who said: If a false witness was brought to Shurayh, he would shake with his heartbeats. And he took off his turban."
"23509","(23509) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan: Concerning a man who bought fodder by weight and took it without weight and it was destroyed. Fodder, and he said: It is from the money he bought.\n He said: And Muhammad said something like this."
"23510","(23510) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If he says: If I do such-and-such, then my servant is free. So he sold it and then did it, saying: He does not owe anything."
"23511","(23511) Abdul Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab. And on the authority of Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Ata: Concerning a man who says to his servant: If you enter the house, you are free. So he sold it and entered the house, then He bought it, they said: He will not be freed."
"23512","(23512) Zayd bin Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Al-Hasan: Concerning a man who says to his servant: If you do such-and-such. Likewise, you are free, and to his wife: you are divorced. He said: If there was a sale or a divorce between them, it would not have taken place."
"23513","(23513) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Hassan bin Salih narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla and Al-Qasim bin Al-Walid. And Ibn Shubarmah: Concerning a man who says: If I do such-and-such, then his boy is free, or his wife is divorced, so he sells the boy, or He divorces the woman, then breaks his oath. They said: He must be emancipated and divorced."
"23514","(23514) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ash-Shu’bi, and on the authority of Ibn Sirin: that Shurayh used to permit Confession in stories."
"23515","(23515) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Furat ibn Abi Bahr narrated to us, on the authority of his father, he said: I witnessed a scroll that was raised to him. He told a story and said: I do not read books."
"23516","(23516) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Hanash, on the authority of Ali: that he made `Ubaid Allah take an oath Ibn Al-Hurr with his evidence."
"23517","(23517) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Hasan bin Salih narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ali: He made Ubaid Allah bin Al-Hurr with his evidence."
"23518","(23518) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Hisham bin Al-Mughirah narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Ashwa’, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: It is ugly. May God make it clear for you if you do not swear to be truthful."
"23519","(23519) Waki’ told us, he said: Malik bin Mughal told us, he said: I said to Al-Sha’abi: Should I make a man swear on his evidence? He said: Yes."
"23520","(23520) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shuraih: He used to swear by The clear statement"
"23521","(23521) Ibn Abi Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: A man rose up against another man with what you made clear, and his opponent said: His right hand is more beloved to me than the witnesses. So he asked him to take an oath and he ate, and Shurayh said: It is miserable that you praised your witnesses and rejected their testimony.\n Abdullah bin Utbah said: I do not give you a right that you do not swear to."
"23522","(23522) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Shubramah and Ibn Abi Layla: In a ship that is chartered. The sea will be broken up, and there will be goods in it: Ibn Shubarmah said: He will not be guaranteed, and Ibn Abi Layla said: He will be guaranteed, and Sufyan said: We do not see any guarantee on it."
"23523","(23523) Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Jabir, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Al-Sha’abi about a man who borrowed He drove an animal and rewarded it with a dirham. Al-Hakam said: The dirham is for him, and Al-Sha’bi said: The dirham is for the owner of the animal."
"23524","(23524) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Sufyan informed us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi: Concerning two men who joined together, So each one brought out ten thousand and did not mix them, so one of them acted according to what he had and issued a fatwa, but he did not see him as a partner, and he said: The decrease and what was lost: on him, and nothing of it is on the other."
"23525","(23525) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, saying: Sufyan said: There will be no partner between them until they mix their wealth."
"23526","(23526) Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, saying: Hassan narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla: He said: In a short story, seek the help of a companion. He pulled the garment and it tore through the garment. He said: He is responsible for the shortcomings."
"23527","(23527) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim: Concerning the sick person, he said: If the heir clears the debt, he is innocent."
"23528","(23528) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Hakam, the same."
"23529","(23529) Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Aisha, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, On the authority of Abraham, he said: Everything is weighed, then like for like, and if there is a difference, then increase and increase, and everything that is measured is like for like. With a similar example, and if it differs, then increase and increase."
"23530","(23530) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: The truth is new and cannot be invalidated by length. abandonment"
"23531","(23531) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan: Concerning a man who stole a slave and sold him to another, and he died in the hands of another. The buyer, he said: The buyer’s money is gone, and the owner of the slave will follow the thief."
"23532","(23532) Omar bin Ayyub told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, who said: I asked Al-Zuhri about a man who buys money with dirhams. Is this a morphology? He said: Yes, so do not leave it until you fulfill it."
"23533","(23533) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, saying: Sufyan informed us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim: Concerning a man who buys a garment. All in all, each garment costs ten dirhams, and some of it is better than others, so some of it contains rags? He said: He will return it with ten.\n Sufyan said something different, saying: He returns it for its value out of all the price. Sufyan said, “And he is more beloved to me.”"
"23534","(23534) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Mufaddal bin Mihalil narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi: Concerning the man giving the call to prayer. To his servant in business, then he sells it to him. He said: He guarantees it."
"23535","(23535) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan bin Salih, who said: I said to Al-Ja’d bin Dhakwan: I saw a narration that said: Should I accept the testimony of the witness against the witness? He said: Yes, if he is just."
"23536","(23536) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Shurayh: He used to reward the testimony of the witness over the witness if he testified. On them."
"23537","(23537) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Shurayh: It was not permissible. The witness is a witness as long as he is alive, even if he is in Yemen."
"23538","(23538) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail al-Azraq, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, who said: He used to say: It is not permissible for the witness to testify against me. The witness until there are two of them."
"23539","(23539) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Muhammad: He saw no harm in fighting."
"23540","(23540) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They used to prefer making money in trade."
"23541","(23541) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Wa’il ibn Dawud, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was asked. He asked: Which earnings are better? He said: A man's work is with his own hands, and every sale is acceptable. (Hakim 10. Bazar 1257)"
"23542","(23542) Hafs told us, he said: I asked Omar what Al-Hasan used to say about watermelon, cucumbers, cucumbers, and roses, and what not. All of them will come out. He said: He used to say: Only what will come out all of them will be bought."
"23543","(23543) Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, saying: Mufaddal narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, he said: I said to Ibrahim: The man should greet in Grapes? He did not see any harm in it. He said: I said: Should I surrender to grapes, should we take a horse? He said: No."
"23544","(23544) Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, saying: Abu Bakr al-Nashili narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Qays, on the authority of Habib ibn Abu Thabit, on the authority of Tawus: A man asked him and said: You have made your maid free. If you reduce her from such-and-such, then she has become afraid. If the season ends before we sell it, do you think we should sell it for less than what you said? He said: If you do not fear the Sultan. Or: Were it not that I fear authority over you."
"23545","(23545) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Muhammad: They did not see any harm in buying A man who sells part of it for cash and part of it for cash: Then he sells it for a profit. They said: He informs his companion of it in a similar manner. He knows"
"23546","(23546) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hurriya, who said: I heard Abu Nadhri say: The honest merchant is in his house. The martyr in the sight of God Almighty on the Day of Resurrection."
"23547","(23547) Ibn Numayr told us, he said: Malik bin Mughul, on the authority of Abu Hamza, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The honest and truthful merchant with The truthful ones and the martyrs.\n He said: So I mentioned that to Abraham, and he said: Hasan spoken the truth, or is he not in jihad? (Tirmidhi 1209, Darqutni 18)"
"23548","(23548) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab: Concerning a man who freed his slave And he made a condition of his service, saying: If he frees him, his condition will be invalidated."
"23549","(23549) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Hayyan Al-Taymi, on the authority of his father: that his neighbor To Shuraih, she entered upon him and her maid of hers was with her, and she said: O father of my mother, you have freed this maid of yours. He said: You have I hear what you say. She said: And I made it a condition that I serve you as long as I live. So Shurayh said: Here it is, if you wish. I did."
"23550","(23550) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Kibran, on the authority of Al-Dahhak: Concerning a woman who emancipated a servant of hers, then made an exception. He said Al-Dahhak: To be freed."
"23551","(23551) Abbad told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Saad bin Al-Akhram, on the authority of His father: A man came to Ibn Masoud and said: I have freed this female slave of mine, and I stipulated that she should follow from me what the slave woman had followed. From her master except the private part, or he said: other than the private part, and when she stiffened her neck, she said: She is free, he said: That is not for her. Take her neck and go with her, and you will have what she stipulated."
"23552","(23552) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jumhan, on the authority of Safina: Umm Salama freed him and stipulated that He must serve the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, as long as he lives. (Abu Dawud 3928 and Ibn Majah 2526)"
"23553","(23553) Abu Bakr al-Hanafi told us, on the authority of al-Dahhak ibn Uthman, who said: Al-Zuhri ordered me, so I wrote a letter about him: That he borrowed gold for a specified period of time for a specified period of good food, or they bought it."
"23554","(23554) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawwi, on the authority of Hammad, who said: If you sold a man food immediately So he took him to his house, then I took him away from him and kept him in his house. If you wish, you could sell some of him for his wife, and his leaders said: Do not buy it from him until you transport it to your home."
"23555","(23555) Abd al-Samad narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: It was said: In a kir of land there is a hundred A balance of female fodder: There is no problem with it."
"23556","(23556) Khaled bin Hayyan told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Marzuq, who said: Ibn Abbas was asked about A man borrowed ancient food and replaced it with modern food? He said: If there is no condition between them, then there is no harm in it."
"23557","(23557) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Saul al-Sarraj, he said: I asked Al-Hasan about a man who helps a man from among the polytheists? He said: Or have you not heard what the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said about the Bedouins?"
"23558","(23558) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Bishr ibn Mansour, on the authority of Hammad: He did not see any harm in buying it. For the people of memory"
"23559","(23559) Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Zayd, on the authority of Abu Abdullah al-Shaqari, on the authority of Ibrahim: Concerning a man who sold something for a term, then the buyer sold it from a man. Did the owner who sold it buy it? He said: If there is no equivalent, then there is no problem."
"23560","(23560) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Zaid, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan: In this matter, if there is no equivalent in it, then there is no problem."
"23561","(23561) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Asim: He sold his sister’s wife For a while, then she ordered him to sell it, so he sold it, so she asked Ibn al-Musayyab? He said: Do you think it is you? I said: I am, he said: That is usury, that is usury, so do not take from it except your capital."
"23562","(23562) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: There is no condition for a dead person."
"23563","(23563) Abd al-Samad narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salama, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of the ruling: Concerning a man who rents out his house for ten years, If he dies before that, the rent is nullified and the loan is nullified.\n Makhoul said: The naked woman shall move away, and the lease shall be invalidated.\n Iyas bin Muawiyah said: They will go to their destination.\n Ayoub said, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin: They will only inherit from that what he had during his lifetime."
"23564","(23564) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Amer: He was asked about a woman who surrendered a slave of hers. A few months ago, so the woman died before that? Amer said to her brother: He is your boy. If you want, you can keep him, and if you want, you can leave him."
"23565","(23565) Ruh bin Ubadah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad: He used to hate the broker’s guarantee."
"23566","(23566) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of al-Zuhri: Concerning a man who took care of a servant of his, then he died. And he has a debt, he said: He will work on it."
"23567","(23567) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’abi, on the authority of Hudhaifa Abi Al-Yaman, who said: I heard Al-Shu’abi say: If a man associates If a man does not criticize, he is not in charge of him, but rather it is a bait that he has given her to him."
"23568","(23568) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri: Concerning a man who sold a boy of his for sheep, and the sheep produced and increased. Then he found a flaw in the boy that had been spoiled by him, and he said: Give him back the sheep’s sheep, or give them to him in their original form. As he took it."
"23569","(23569) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Muhammad: Concerning a man who pawns the Qur’an by display, they said: It is not read. And if its owner gives permission, and if it is about a sale and its owner permits it, then it is read in it, otherwise it is not read in it."
"23570","(23570) Muhammad ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: Muhammad was reluctant to rent land. And he will build in it some of its reward."
"23571","(23571) Muhammad bin Abi Adi narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: Muhammad hated for the resident to hasten the reward. Something"
"23572","(23572) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: There was a man who rewarded himself for a year for a thousand dirhams. He said: So he said to me: Ask Muhammad, for they hastened to come to me, so I asked him? He said: I don't know of any harm in it."
"23573","(23573) Muhammad bin Abi Adi narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: Al-Qasim bin Muhammad used to dispute with a judge and he decided. Ali, then that judge was removed, then someone else came, and he was ruling for the judge, and he was told: If you dispute with him, and he said: No, I argued before a judge and he ruled against me."
"23574","(23574) Azhar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: There is no harm in a garment if a man says: If you take all of it Then for ten, and if you take half of it, then for eleven."
"23575","(23575) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan bin Salih, on the authority of Issa bin Abi Ezza, who said: Amer was He permits the sealed letter to come from the judge."
"23576","(23576) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Omar bin Abi Zaydah, who said: We brought a letter from the judge of Kufa to Iyas bin Muawiyah, I came when Iyas had been deposed and Al-Hasan had been judged, so I handed over my letter to him and he accepted it and did not ask me about it. So he opened it, then spread it out, and found within it two witnesses bearing witness against a man from the people of Basra for five hundred dirhams. So he said to a man who was in charge of him: Take this to Ibn Ziyad, and tell him: Send it to so-and-so, son of so-and-so, and take it from him. Five hundred dirhams, so he paid her for this. He said: So he went with me and he did so."
"23577","(23577) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A letter from a judge to a judge is permissible."
"23578","(23578) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Issa bin Abi Ezzah, who said: Al-Sha’bi used to ask The witness is that he will bring someone whom he will purify."
"23579","(23579) Hammad bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Sinan: That a man bought a wall of pomegranates for eight hundred dirhams, so he sold of it for twenty dirhams, then he sold what was left for a profit, so he informed its owner, so he disputed with him and went to the market keeper, and he exonerated him. From us\n He said: So I asked Al-Qasim, is he safe? They said: This is not suitable."
"23580","(23580) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a man buys an animal and finds a defect in its tooth and wants He rejected it, for he swore by God that it was because of her tooth that he rejected it, and if it was a defect other than that, he did not swear."
"23581","(23581) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Hanash ibn al-Harith, on the authority of Ali ibn Mudrik al-Nakha’i: That a man bought a female slave from a man. He did not find any molars on it, so he disputed with Shurayh, and Shurayh said: I made it clear to you that he sold it and it had no molars. Otherwise, he swears by God that he sold her to her while she had molars."
"23582","(23582) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, who said: I asked Abraham about shoes with two soles without any reward. So he spoiled them? He said: I hate that I guarantee him, and I have not given him any reward."
"23583","(23583) Ahmad bin Bashir narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Shubarmah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, something similar."
"23584","(23584) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi: Concerning a man who took food from another man, meaning He usurped him, he said: The same is upon him."
"23585","(23585) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Issa Al-Kabbat told us, he said: I asked Saeed bin Al-Musayyab about a man. He hired a porter to carry food, so he placed a load of it on his family, then said: Look at what you are selling, and count it. Ali? He said: Saeed: He has food like yours."
"23586","(23586) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: A Sharih used to swear an absolute oath regarding the man being sued. His father is in debt, so if he swears, otherwise he will take it from him, and your father will have a debt owed by a person. You will claim it and establish proof. If You swore with your evidence, otherwise he will not give it to you."
"23587","(23587) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He swears in these two chapters on his knowledge."
"23588","(23588) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shurayh: That he used to swear to the Prophet While he was absent and present, he said: So I said to Amir: What do you think if a man claimed money against my father that I had no knowledge of, would I have to Should I swear to you? He said: Yes, so we strongly denied that. He said: Refuse the oath to the one who knows it better than you.\n He said: Amer used to take it."
"23589","(23589) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A man did not swear by himself unless he swore at all times, and he did not His guardian other than him was sworn on his knowledge."
"23590","(23590) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: A man takes an oath regarding what he claims. On his father, on his knowledge."
"23591","(23591) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’abi, on the authority of Ammarah ibn Abi Hafsa, who said: Two men disputed with Al-Hasan, and he said to him: He made him swear on a right that belonged to his father, and his father did not bear witness. He said: Then Al-Hasan said: Would any sensible person swear on this?"
"23592","(23592) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri: on the authority of a man who acquires forbidden money. He said: If he is pleased that If he disavows it, let him leave it."
"23593","(23593) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Malik ibn Dinar, who said: A man said to Ata’ ibn Abi Rabah: A man acquired money from Forbidden? He said: To return it to his family, but if he does not know his family then let him give it in charity, and I do not know how that will save him from His sin"
"23594","(23594) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, saying: Malik ibn Dinar claimed that a man asked a gift and he said: I was a boy. So I acquired wealth in various ways that I do not like, so I want to repent? He said: Return it to its family. He said: I do not know them. He said: Give it in charity, for there is no reward for you in that, and I do not know. Will she accept her burden or not? He said: And he asked Mujahid? He said like that."
"23595","(23595) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Sa’d, who said: A man asked Abu Ja’far about a man who said: A friend of mine. He acquired illicit wealth and mixed everything with it, whether his family or theirs. Then he realized what was in it, so he began Hajj. And next to this house, what do you think of it? He said: I think that he should fear God and then not do it again."
"23596","(23596) Hafs told us, on the authority of Suleiman Abi Abdullah, who said: Al-Hasan said: Whoever keeps money from a man, or steals from a man Money, and he wanted to return it to him from a place he did not know, so he delivered it to him: there is no problem."
"23597","(23597) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid al-Tawil, on the authority of Anas bin Malik and Iyas bin Muawiyah: They were asked about a Mamluk who was among three people. So one of them wrote off his share, and one of them freed his share, and the slave died and left behind money? So Anas and Iyas decided: Whatever he left behind was with them as it should be."
"23598","(23598) Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Musa ibn Ali ibn Rabah, who said: I asked Al-Zuhri about someone who married a free man. So he had her children, and he bought a maidservant and had her children. He died, and some of the entitlements of either of them remained for him while he worked. He stayed on? He said: His sons are those of his female slave."
"23599","(23599) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, he said: I asked Hammad about a man who is in the house for a while and people come and stay. What is clear is that it was their grandfather’s? He said: No, until they bear witness that it is His today."
"23600","(23600) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Al-Harith, he said: If the house was in a row, the people wanted to divide it up. It is divided according to the inheritance, the inheritance of the dead person in the wrong, if one of the heirs, or someone else, claims a claim. Above what he receives from the inheritance: He has the clear proof of what so-and-so claimed, or that he gave charity to me, or it was given to me. Or he sold me for such-and-such, and if I asked for a woman or a husband who belonged to some of the dead people, then he will pay the clear price. That so-and-so inherited so-and-so, or so-and-so inherited so-and-so, or the person in the line of inheritance died before her or him before him. I inherited from him, so he is taking his rights.\n And if a man from the descendants of the one who made a mistake claims it and denies those in whose hands its share is due, then the one who claims What is clear is that so-and-so died before so-and-so, and so-and-so inherited from him, and I inherited from him after him.\n If the heirs acknowledge that the owner of the house had a woman, and her family claimed her share, then it remains their responsibility. And if they say: He divorced her before death, then what is clear to them is that he divorced her, otherwise the inheritance is obligatory. No\n And if the house is purchased and is in the hands of a people, then it belongs to those who are in their hands. If a person claims it, he will do so. It is clear that he has a right to it."
"23601","(23601) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer, who said: They have not narrated anything more astonishing to me than their saying: “Yashud.” He is his today."
"23602","(23602) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Al-Harith and Hammad, who said: If a man said to another man: Go to the door of the house and Five hundred dirhams, they said: He had that."
"23603","(23603) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Mughiriya and Ash-Shu’bi: Concerning a man who deceived the child of her fornication into his oath, so he freed him, then he freed him. It was learned that after that, they said: It is permissible for him to be freed, and he will be freed from the wealth of the one who seduced him, and loyalty is to him."
"23604","(23604) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Hujayr, on the authority of Iyas ibn Muawiyah: Concerning a man who was bargaining with another man. With something, another man came and wanted to bargain with him, so the bargaining man rebuked him, and Omar bin Al-Khattab saw that she was a partner."
"23605","(23605) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad: That a man sold a slave of his for the cut of his hair. So he disputed with him to Shurayh and said: You concealed the matter and hid it, but his response was not sufficient."
"23606","(23606) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, who said: I asked Ata’: I buy for a thousand dirhams, so I say before the contract: Shall I make it a hundred dinars? He said: No problem."
"23607","(23607) Khaled bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Bilal, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever deceives us is not one of us. (Muslim 164. Abu Dawud 3446)"
"23608","(23608) Ishaq Al-Azraq told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Muhammad, that they both said: Cheating is forbidden."
"23609","(23609) Al-Aswad bin Amir narrated to us, he said: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Isa, on the authority of Juma bin Umair, on the authority of Amir, On the authority of Abu Burda, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: He who deceives us is not one of us. (Bukhari 2817. Ahmad 3/45)"
"23610","(23610) Ishaq Al-Azraq narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan: He had ordered the people of Mudarab to make There is a known month among them, in which they seek reward."
"23611","(23611) Ali narrated to us, on the authority of Hafs, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Talha, who said: If the witnesses differ as to what is said and the principle is the same: It's okay"
"23612","(23612) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zayed, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Hanash, on the authority of Ali, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: If two men are suing over you, do not hear what the first says, until you hear what the other says, for you will see How do you spend it?\n Ali said: I am still a judge after her. (Tirmidhi 1331. Abu Dawud 3577)"
"23613","(23613) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Qasim and Amir, that they said: Do not accept your adversaries from an adversary. Until his opponent is present."
"23614","(23614) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, saying: Hassan narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: A man takes from his son’s wealth whatever he wants, except private parts."
"23615","(23615) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, saying: Hassan narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Al-Hakam like that."
"23616","(23616) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: I said to Al-Hasan: The man takes his son’s maidservant? He said: No."
"23617","(23617) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Hamza, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: The father is free from His son’s wealth, except for private parts."
"23618","(23618) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Iyas bin Muawiyah, he said: He used to say: The owners of houses have more right to the annihilation of their houses, and the owners of two lands have more right to the destruction of their land."
"23619","(23619) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of his leaders, who said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote: He who is victorious. Water is on something, so it is for him."
"23620","(23620) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Omar Mawla Ghafari, he said: I asked Saeed bin Al-Musayyab about two men. They entered into a partnership, and one of them paid money on behalf of the owner of all the price, so they went to Medina and sold a group of land, and they made a profit, but a group remained, so he said The one who gave money to its owner: If you wish, you may pay what is left while you are in charge of your partnership, and if you wish, you may withdraw from it and from its profits. And I absolved you? He said: This is not permissible.\n I asked Al-Qasim and he said: Like that."
"23621","(23621) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Sallam bin Abi Dhayal, who said: I asked Al-Hasan about two men who bought some goods. So he sold it at a profit for cash and cash? Then one of them said to his friend: Give me my capital, so whatever remains is yours. He said: His good thought."
"23622","(23622) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Sulaiman al-Taymi, on the authority of Ibn Sirin: Concerning a man who is paid off from gambling. He said: No problem. Al-Hasan said about a man who pays off interest: There is no harm in him."
"23623","(23623) Qubaysah narrated to us, saying: Harun al-Barbari narrated to us, saying: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about a man who paid money to a man. He speculated and testified about it, then the man came and wanted to take his money from him, so he said: I paid it to you, so he said The ruling: It is clear that he pushed him to it as he testified about it, and Hammad said: It is confirmed in it just as it is confirmed in it. Like him"
"23624","(23624) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ash-Shu’bi, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: It is permissible for a servant to acknowledge what he accomplished in it. His family"
"23625","(23625) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim: He used to permit the servant’s statement regarding His family gave him permission to do so."
"23626","(23626) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Zaid narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yasar: He was asked about a man who had a burden of righteousness over another man? He said: This is a ball that I have measured. Should he take it with its full measure? He said: If he wants, he can take it by his own measure."
"23627","(23627) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Husayn al-Mu’allim, on the authority of Makhoul: Concerning a man who said to another man: My servant is yours as long as I live. So if you die, he is free. He said: It is permissible."
"23628","(23628) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan: Concerning a man who bought a large amount of food from another man and gave him the money, then He went to pick up the food but did not finish it. He said: So that the owner of the food would return to him the price of what was left on his share of what he had bought. He said: And it was Muhammad hates him."
"23629","(23629) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj ibn Arta, on the authority of Abu Ja`far al-Bajli, who said: A man entered the bathroom. So he gave him a reward for entering the bathroom. He said: And he gave him his clothes to hold. He said: The clothes were lost. He said: So he quarreled with him. To Shurayh, he said: Then Shurayh said: Did you give me permission to hold the clothes? He said: No, but I gave him permission to enter the bathroom, so Shurayh said to him: Get up, there is nothing wrong with you."
"23630","(23630) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim: Concerning a man who says: If you do such-and-such, then with that. And if you do such-and-such, then with that. He said: There is no problem with it as a rental."
"23631","(23631) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Zaid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Mujahid: That a man was sent to Aisha in Basra. Of the dinars that she owed to Aisha, the Mother of the Believers. When the people ended close to Medina, a sky struck them, and it was lost. Then the people went on and came to Medina, and the man looked at the book, then he made something like dinars and wrote on it, then he came With the letter and the package to Aisha, and a people passed by that house, and they found the package with writing on it, so they brought it to Aisha, so she sent this to the owner of the first dinars, and said to him: Tell me the news about the dinars, and he said to her: The news is in The book. She said: Believe me. So he told her the news. She said: You wanted to feed me something that is not lawful for me."
"23632","(23632) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’: Concerning a man who bought goods from a man. He said: If I will bring you the price for such-and-such. He said, “It is not a sale.”"
"23633","(23633) Al-Dahhak ibn Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Suleiman, the client of Al-Barasa’, informed me. He said: I sold from Ibn Umar, either a commodity or a sale, and he said: If our expenditure reaches three, then the commodity is ours, and if our expenditure does not reach three, then no sale. Between us and you, we will receive a sale in the future."
"23634","(23634) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, he said: It was from the origin of Al-Hasan’s statement that he saw no harm. Which of the zeros is correct, with the two pronouns of the broken zeros, and he was asked about a knife with two knives? He saw no harm in it."
"23635","(23635) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Salamah, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Armor was sold for shields."
"23636","(23636) Suwayd bin Amr told us, he said: Abu Awani told us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim and Ash-Shu’bi: The man has a witness with his right hand. He said: It is only permissible for two men to bear witness, or one man and two women.\n Amer said: Even though the people of Medina say: “The two witnesses are witnesses with the right hand of the seeker.”"
"23637","(23637) Hammad bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: It is an innovation, and he was the first to judge it. Bye Mu'awiyah"
"23638","(23638) Ali bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Jahm bin Abi Al-Jaham, he said: Whoever heard narrated to me Abdullah bin Jaafar narrates: Ali did not attend his opponents, and he used to say: She had a burden to attend her. Satan, so he assigned his disputes to Aqeel, and when he grew up and grew up, he turned them over to me, and Ali used to say: What has been decided is to my representative. So, let me do it, and whatever my representative has decided upon me, let me do it."
"23639","(23639) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin, on the authority of Shuraih, who said, “The promise of Muslim, even if He did not stipulate: no disease, no deceit, no malice, and no shame."
"23640","(23640) Ibn Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Asim, who said: A man said to Amir: She bought a horse, paid its price, and shared it. A man, and the horse died, and he said: Count your horse."
"23641","(23641) Abd al-Rahman al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Amr, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas He said: Whoever goes to a man to fulfill his rights, a good deed will be recorded for him, with every good step he made."
"23642","(23642) Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Huraim told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad: Al-Hussein bin Ali passed by a shepherd who was grazing, so he brought him a sheep and he gave it to him, and he said to him: Are you free or a slave? He said: A slave, so he returned it to him, and he said: It is mine, so he accepted it from him, then he bought it and bought the sheep, and freed them and made The sheep belong to him."
"23643","(23643) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Shurayh: If the witness was accused, he would not He asks him until he gets up."
"23644","(23644) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Sayyar, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi: That a man cut a man’s fur, so they quarreled to a point, and he said: A patch in place of a patch."
"23645","(23645) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Ash-Shu’bi, on the authority of Masruq: Concerning a man who pierces The fur, he said: He only has to wear a patch."
"23646","(23446) Zaid bin Hubab told us, he said: Husayn bin Waqid told me, he said: Othman Abu Al-Manazil, my nephew, told me. Shurayh, on the authority of Shurayh: He did not allow the testimony of the owner of a pigeon, nor the owner of the pigeons."
"23647","(23647) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Muhazam, on the authority of Abu Hurairah: He was not He approves the testimony of those who drink alcohol."
"23648","(23648) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: There was no Mut’hab except in inside his house"
"23649","(23649) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If a specified share of his property is sold, it is permissible, but if it is not Named, not permissible."
"23650","(23650) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of `Ubaidah and Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, a similar matter."
"23651","(23651) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Al-Saab bin Jathama, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: There is no fever except for God and His Messenger. (Bukhari 3012, Ibn Hibban 136)"
"23652","(23652) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: No. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, about withholding the surplus of water in order to prevent the surplus of kidneys."
"23653","(23653) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ibn Tawus: That his father hated selling kala in His germination"
"23654","(23654) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Omar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar: Omar’s father-in-law The Lord is the best of charity."
"23655","(23655) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Thawr al-Shami narrated to us, on the authority of Hariz bin Uthman, on the authority of Abu Khidash, on the authority of a man among the companions of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Muslims are partners in three: both. And water and fire. (Abu Dawud 3472. Ahmad 5/364)"
"23656","(23656) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Hisham bin Saad narrated to us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam: That the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace And peace be upon him, it is permissible for Arabs to sell."
"23657","(23657) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Muslim, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Misra, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab He said: There is no deposit in your land, fodder, or food, and the deposit is in something else."
"23658","(23658) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: He did not see any harm in the Arabs."
"23659","(23659) Yazeed told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin: He did not see any harm in a man giving The ferryman, the boatman, or someone else, says: If you bring him to such-and-such and such-and-such, and he tells you, he is yours."
"23660","(23660) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Hamza bin Abdullah bin Omar bin Al-Khattab, he said: We used to sell clothes between the hands of Abdullah bin Omar: Whoever ransomed ransoms, ransoms a dirham, let him not command us or He forbade us."
"23661","(23661) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Aslam: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, permitted the Arabs to Selling"
"23662","(23662) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Farukh: that Nafi’ ibn Abd al-Harith bought the prison house. From Safwan bin Umayyah for four thousand dirhams. If Omar is satisfied, then the sale is his, and if Omar is not satisfied, then four hundred. To Safwan."
"23663","(23663) Zayd ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Hisham and Ibn Aoun narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: He used to say Concerning a man who rents a house and a ship, and says: If I come to such-and-such and such-and-such, then it is yours. He said: If he does not come to him, So it is for him."
"23664","(23644) Abdullah bin Mubarak told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’. On the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father: They both disliked the Arabs in selling."
"23665","(23645) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Musa ibn Ali, who said: I asked al-Zuhri about an enemy vehicle that was thrown by the wind. People? He said: It is for the one who took his spoils, and there is a fifth in it."
"23666","(23666) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Ghayath, who said: Al-Hasan was asked about a ship sinking in the sea, with goods on it. For a captive people? He said: Whatever the sea throws on its shore belongs to its owner, and whoever dives on something and extracts it, it is his."
"23667","(23667) Zayd bin Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salama, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’: In the sea he throws the belongings, he said: By the position of the piece, you can identify it."
"23668","(23668) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Ghalib Abi Al-Dhail, on the authority of Kulayb Al-Jarmiyy: That he bore witness to Ali. Butchers, about blowing. Meaning: in meat."
"23669","(23669) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Al-Ahwas ibn Hakim, on the authority of Rashid ibn Saad, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade May the peace and blessings of God be upon him about blowing into meat for sale."
"23670","(23670) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham: He did not dislike the Qur’an with the Qur’an. exchanged"
"23671","(23671) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: There is no harm in exchanging one Qur’an for another Qur’an."
"23672","(23672) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: There is no harm in the Qur’an for the Qur’an, and between them is ten dirhams."
"23673","(23673) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The Qur’an is not divided in inheritance. For the readers of Ahl al-Bayt."
"23674","(23674) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Omar said: Whoever indulges in three things There were times when it did not work, so he changed from it to another."
"23675","(23675) Hafs told us, on the authority of Musa bin Umair, who said: I asked the ruling about a man who bought a female slave and then had intercourse with her. Should I sell it at a profit? He said: No, until he explains it."
"23676","(23676) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Khalid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Shurayh used to greet Ali. Opponents"
"23677","(23677) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of someone who heard Ibn Sirin detest it if one of the negotiators inherited something. And his companion shares it with him."
"23678","(23678) Abdou narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab: He did not see any harm in A man buys the butchers’ arrows before they are divided."
"23679","(23679) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan: Concerning a man who buys property on the condition that he free them, but no He does? He said: If he frees him, otherwise return him."
"23680","(23680) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Awn, on the authority of Ibn Sirin: that Omar approved the testimony of the eunuch’s testimony to Ali. Ibn Maz'un."
"23681","(23681) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Muhammad bin Muslim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: No. He should sell with credit and buy with it, and not sell for cash and buy with credit, and there is no harm in that. He sells with credit and buys with cash."
"23682","(23682) Abu Osama narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us: that Muwarriq al-Ijali used to pass by the ten man and ask him for food."
"23683","(23683) Abu Usama told us, he said: Hisham told us, he said: Al-Hassan hated to ask him for food, but he did not see it. It is unfortunate if he feeds him if he eats."
"23684","(23684) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Hakim bin Jubayr, who said: We brought Sa`id bin Jubayr at the bottom of Euphrates, so he sent the tax collectors to the owner of the bridge: If you have anything, feed us. They fed us, and he ate with us."
"23685","(23685) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Husayn: A man broke a man’s drum, so he quarreled with him to a point. He did not guarantee anything from him."
"23686","(23686) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Uthman al-Shahham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin: He hated it and it was mentioned in his presence. The reward of the auctioneer."
"23687","(23687) Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi told us, on the authority of Yazid ibn Ata, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Hajjar ibn Abjar: That a man, He said to Ali: He is gone, and by God, my money. Then Ali said to him: You lost it. Why did you not take it from him with his knowledge?"
"23688","(23688) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan: Concerning a man who had money from another man, so he took it. And he said: There is no harm in it, even if it is silver after it has been weighed by weight for weight."
"23689","(23689) Saul bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad: He did not see any harm in listening to people."
"23690","(23690) Ubaidullah ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Sufyan informed us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ali ibn Mudarrak: that Al-Dahhak ibn A Qays went to her regarding a slave girl in whom he found an empyema, which is an old disease and it is known that it is not something that happens. The seller was judged accordingly.\n Sufyan said: Al-Dahhak’s statement is more beloved to me than Shurayh’s statement: If he knew that it would not happen that he would be rejected. The buyer must swear an oath that he did not see it before he bought it, and was not satisfied with it after he saw it."
"23691","(23691) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Fudail, who said: A man gave me a dinar with which to buy land for himself, and it perished. So I said to the embalmer: Every place is in its place. So I mentioned it to Abraham, and he said: As it happened to you."
"23692","(23692) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Imran Al-Khayyat, who said: A woman gave me money to buy for her. With it, a weight of it was destroyed. So I mentioned it to Abraham, and he said: Make its place."
"23693","(23693) Mu’tamir and Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The Messenger has no liability."
"23694","(23694) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Ali and Abdullah, who said: There is no guarantee on a trustworthy person."
"23695","(23695) Omar told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The trustworthy person is not liable unless he violates it."
"23696","(23696) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, who said: It is disliked for a mudarib to say to his companion: I prefer you. Twenty dirhams, or thirty, and he sees nothing wrong with saying: I prefer you by a third, or a quarter, or a sixth."
"23697","(23697) Abd al-Wahhab bin Ata’ told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin al-Musayyab, and Ibn Sirin: They did not see anything wrong with a man giving another man Mudarab money and saying: From it you will get a profit of a thousand dirhams."
"23698","(23698) Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata’ told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of al-Hasan: He used to dislike that except To give him a third, or a quarter, or a fifth."
"23699","(23699) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: The profit of money is guaranteed. He said: They interpreted it as: The man takes from A man is speculating money and says: I guarantee you, and you get half or a third of the profit."
"23700","(23700) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aliya, she said: I was sitting with Aisha and she came to her. A woman said: O Mother of the Believers, I found a lost sheep, so what do you command me to do with it? She said: Introduce me, feed me, and milk me. Then she came back and asked her? She said: Do you command me to order you to sell it or slaughter it? This is not for you."
"23701","(23701) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Zayd bin Jubayr, who said: I was sitting with Ibn Umar when a man came to him and said: I found a lost woman, so he said: Be kind to her and chant, so he said: What is the matter with me if I drink some of its milk? Ibn Omar said: I don’t think you have anything wrong with that."
"23702","(23702) Yahya bin Abi Zaydi told us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Bilal, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed Ibn Al-Musayyab: A man said to him: I found a lost camel, should I let him shoot his camels? He said: No."
"23703","(23703) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no profit for guaranteed money. The interpretation of this said: A man takes speculative money from another man, and says: I guarantee you, and you get half the profit, or a third of it."
"23704","(23704) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer: Concerning a man who buys goods and sees a defect in them, then... He offers it for sale: he does not have the right to return it."
"23705","(23705) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of `Ubaydah, on the authority of Abraham, the same."
"23706","(23706) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: If a man offers the commodity for sale after He sees the disease passed on him."
"23707","(23707) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: If a man buys The commodity, then he put it on sale, or offered it for sale after the defect occurred."
"23708","(23708) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir and Abu Ja’far, who said: They hated the man to sell rather than take. dinar and so on."
"23709","(23709) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham, the same."
"23710","(23710) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: He asked him about a man who buys land for such-and-such. A dirham, a dinar for ten.\n He said: Masruq told me, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: Two deals in one deal are not valid."
"23711","(23711) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer, who said: A mother who has not menstruated should not be returned unless the one who purchased it stipulates that"
"23712","(23712) Sharik told us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer, who said: I asked him about a man who claims different things against another man? He said: He will make him swear on something by something."
"23713","(23713) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani: On the authority of a man who entrusted sheep and they bred with him, so he sold them. He said: It was worth its value on the day he sold it."
"23714","(23714) Shababi bin Siwar narrated to us, saying: Laith bin Saad narrated to us, on the authority of Bukair, on the authority of Iyad bin Abdullah bin Sa’d, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, who said: A man was afflicted during the time of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, regarding the fruits he bought, and he multiplied His religion, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Give alms to him, so the people gave alms to him, but that did not amount to fulfillment. His religion, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Take what you find, and you have nothing but that. Meaning: fines.\n(Muslim 1191. Abu Dawud 3463)"
"23715","(23715) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Zam’i narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ibn Ka’b bin Malik, on the authority of his father: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, passed by him while he was accompanying a man for two periods, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to the man: Thus, in his hand, that is, he put away half of it, and the man said to him: Yes, O Messenger of God, and he said: Give him what remains of his right.\n(Bukhari 457, Abu Dawud 3590)"
"23716","(23716) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Abu Salih al-Hanafi, that a people were forced to Debts in the time of Omar ibn al-Khattab, so Omar wrote to his handler: They should defer a third until easy, and put aside a third, and make A third, so they did it."
"23717","(23717) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim: He disliked for a man to say To the man: Buy this dinar from me and I will pay it for you."
"23718","(23718) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: Ibn al-Zubayr forbade selling palm trees at random."
"23719","(23719) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Hamid Al-Araj, on the authority of Suleiman bin Atiq, on the authority of Jabir: That the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, forbade the sale of palm trees for years. (Abu Dawud 33671, Muslim 1178)"
"23720","(23720) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir: That the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade About reconciliation\n(Muslim 1175. Abu Dawud 3397)"
"23721","(23721) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ali, who said: I was entrusted with the truthfulness of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted me, so I came to Mahmoud bin Labid and asked him? He said: Omar had an orphan with him, so he sold his money for three years."
"23722","(23722) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, who said: I told him: Ibrahim hated selling palm trees. The two years? He said: He hated what was easier than this."
"23723","(23723) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of Sa’d, the client of Omar: that Asad ibn Hudair died with his burden on him. debt, so Omar sold the fruit of his land for two years."
"23724","(23724) Ubaidullah narrated to us, saying: Sufyan said: There is no going back in your case except with the judge.\n Ibn Abi Layla said: He will return without the judge."
"23725","(23725) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: When he confessed something to the judge and then he was an infidel, he was taken. By his approval, except the punishment."
"23726","(23726) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer: About two men managing the matter, and one of them said: To its owner: If you swear, it is yours. He said: If he swears, then it is his."
"23727","(23727) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ubadā bin Muslim, on the authority of Muhammad bin Misra, who said: I heard a peacock being sold. Tiger skins, elephant bones, and their purchases."
"23728","(23728) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Rabi’a, on the authority of Al-Hasan: He saw no harm in buying or selling tiger skins."
"23729","(23729) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin: They saw no harm in buying tusks. Elephants, and there is no harm in selling them."
"23730","(23730) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: There is no harm in trading in ivory."
"23731","(23731) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Yazid bin Ibrahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin: Concerning a man who paid yarn to a weaver. So he spoiled it, he said: Shurayh used to say: “Establish the clear evidence,” but he spoiled it. So when he established the clear evidence, he said to the weaver: Give him something like his flirtation."
"23732","(23732) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, who said: I handed over my mother’s yarn to a weaver and he ruined it. So I asked Abraham? He said: He guarantees."
"23733","(23733) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, who said: Omar said: No one will sell in your market except a sensible person. Selling"
"23734","(23734) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Zazan, who said: Two men entrusted a woman and said to her: No. You give it to one of us so that we can meet with you. Then they set off and disappeared, and one of them came to her and said: Give it to me. She said goodbye to me, because my companion had died, so she refused until he went to her a lot, then she gave it to him, then the other one came after that and said: My deposit came and she said: Your friend came and mentioned that you had died, so he took your deposit from me. So they went up to Omar, and when He told her the story. Omar said to her: I have never seen you except that you were safe. The woman said: O Commander of the Faithful, appoint Ali as superior. Between me and him, he said to Ali: Decide between them, Ali. Ali said: This is what is entrusted to me, and he has You ordered her not to give it to either of you until you both met there, so bring your companion to me, but he did not guarantee her. He said: So they saw They only wanted to take the woman's money."
"23735","(23735) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said regarding Al-Mudharib, he passes by the tenth and gives him a gift. And he makes for him a jar of oil. He said, “He counts it as part of the profit. If there is no profit, then it is from the capital.” He said: “He makes With money for money."
"23736","(23736) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Hammad: Concerning a man who sells a concubine that has been born from him, and a man buys her. Then he will fall on her and she will give birth to him also. He said: She will be returned to the first, and she will have a friend like her, and her children will be from the other. According to her status, they will be freed for freeing her, and the other will take her price from the first, even if one of them knows that it is not suitable. He was punished, and if they both knew, they would be punished."
"23737","(23737) Azhar al-Samman narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad: Concerning a man who sold property to another man and he placed it with him, so he sold it to him. The buyer, he said: The profit goes to the first."
"23738","(23738) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad: Concerning a man who bought some goods from a man, so he went and brought him a porter. He transported it, and found that its owner had sold it. He said: If he finds something with his own, he will take it, and if it is gone, it will not be appreciated. There is nothing for him, and his profit goes to the one who sold him."
"23739","(23739) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, he said: She witnessed the ruling. He asked Abraham but he did not answer him."
"23740","(23740) Waki’ narrated to us, he said: Zakaria narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, on the authority of Abu Hariri, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: The mortgage is taken if it is mortgaged, and the milk of pearls is drunk if it is mortgaged, and upon the one who rides it. And he drinks his expenses. (Bukhari 2511, Abu Dawud 3521)"
"23741","(23741) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us. On the authority of Abbad bin Al-Awwam, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi: Concerning a servant who took a mortgage. He said: I spent on the mortgager."
"23742","(23742) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Mufaddal bin Mihalil narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: The bettor paid the ransom to the bettor."
"23743","(23743) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: I heard Hassan bin Salih, saying: The mortgage is paid by the mortgagee because it is in Guarantee\n And Abu Hanifa said: “Ali is the bettor.”"
"23744","(23744) Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: I asked a partner: Who should pay for the animal’s expenses if it is a colt? He said: On the bettor."
"23745","(23745) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Sa’d, who said: I asked Abu Ja’far about a man who bought food from him. So he gives me some of it, then he breaks it off and finds nothing to give me, so he says: “Sell me some of your food so that I can give it to you?” He said: Do not approach this, this is clear usury."
"23746","(23746) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Omar bin Amir, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar: Concerning a man who hired He hired him for more than what he hired him for, he said, credit goes to the first."
"23747","(23747) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ibn Umar: He hated it."
"23748","(23748) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim: Concerning a man who occupies the House and is disgraced more than He hired him and said: He will return the favor."
"23749","(23749) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Ali bin Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Sa`id bin Al-Musayyab, Abu Salma bin Abdul-Rahman, Urwa bin Al-Zubair, and Sulayman bin Yasar: Concerning the man who rents the house. So he rented it out for more than what he rented it for, so two people allowed it, and two people disapproved of it."
"23750","(23750) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Do not take any leftover animal. You rent it, but there is no home."
"23751","(23751) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Talhah, on the authority of Iyas bin Muawiyah, that he said: If you hire a boy or a smoker, do not You rent it for more than you rented it."
"23752","(23752) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Abu Hilal narrated to us, saying: I heard Shahr bin Hawshab hate that a man should be hired. The thing is rented for more than what he paid for."
"23753","(23753) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: It is forbidden."
"23754","(23754) Waki’ told us, he said: Shu’ba told us, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Abraham, he said: It is usury."
"23755","(23755) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, who said: I asked him about a man who rents a thing and he rents it out. He did more than what he hired him for, but he saw nothing wrong with it. Then I asked him about it after he thought about it."
"23756","(23756) Omar bin Ayyub told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of Maymun: He hated it."
"23757","(23757) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim: He disliked for a man to hire The house, then he rents it out for more than he rented it for.\n He said: I said to Abraham: If he rewards her with more, to whom will the reward be? He said: To its owner."
"23758","(23758) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus bin Ubaid, on the authority of Ibn Sirin: He hated it."
"23759","(23759) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: Our Kufan companions used to hate us and say: : Why did we buy or sell? So why should we eat his money?"
"23760","(23760) Ibn Aliya narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, and Ibn Omar: They used to hate that if a man rented something, he would rent it out for more than what he rented it for."
"23761","(23761) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Awf, who said: Hisham bin Hubaira used to judge: one who rents something and then He rewarded him with more than what he hired him for, for that bounty belongs to his Lord."
"23762","(23762) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Al-Zabarqan, on the authority of Ibrahim, like the hadith of Waki’, on the authority of Mansur."
"23763","(23763) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, he said: I asked Al-Sha’bi and Al-Hakam about a man who mutilates camels, then tortures them. For more than he rented it for? He said: There is no problem if he works on it himself, or hires a worker for it."
"23764","(23764) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata’: He was asked about a man who multiplied camels and then forced them. With more than that? He said: He hesitated for a while, then said: I don’t see anything wrong with it, in your opinion."
"23765","(23765) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Zam’iya, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: There is no harm if you choose a verse that He is rewarded with more than his reward."
"23766","(23766) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Hisham ibn Hubayra: He disliked it unless it was used, or He lives in the house, or he lives in some of it."
"23767","(23767) Ibn Abi Ghaniyy told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Hikam, he said: If a man rents the house, he rents out part of it. He paused some of it and said: No problem."
"23768","(23768) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Amir: He disliked it unless he put it right. Something"
"23769","(23769) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Rabi’, Mubarak, and Abu Hilal narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, saying: There is no harm in him renting The man buys something, then rents it out for more."
"23770","(23770) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, that he saw no harm in a man renting a house and then renting it out. For more than what he hired him for."
"23771","(23771) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam, he said: If a chisel was handed to him, or he passed by and he treated him with more Whatever he hired you for, there is no problem."
"23772","(23772) Ishaq bin Mansour narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Rashid, on the authority of Makhoul: He did not see any harm in renting The hired worker or the thing for more than what he hired for it."
"23773","(23773) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Ubaidah, who said: Choosing among young men is a ruling."
"23774","(23774) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Bukair al-Adhim, on the authority of Ali, who said: It is a ruling."
"23775","(23775) Hashim told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan. And Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham: They disliked that a man should give to a man an animal, or a boy, or a house, and he should say: What? Whatever you gain, it is between you and me."
"23776","(23776) Hisham told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: It was said to him: There are people who are slavers and owners of animals. Someone called his animal stable: Khorasan and Sijistan! Then he comes to the market and says: She came from Khorasan and Sijistan. He said: Abraham thought that."
"23777","(23777) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He saw no harm in selling dates to someone who would grind them. Until he buys it."
"23778","(23778) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim: He disliked her carrying the dead to someone. He considers it permissible to eat it, and he sees no harm in hiring someone to transport it for him."
"23779","(23779) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim: Concerning a man who bought merchandise for such and such a month, and for He bought two contracts for such-and-such, so he redeemed the sale, saying: He has the equivalent of two-eighths up to the furthest of the two terms."
"23780","(23780) Ahmad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Wahib, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: Whoever sold two Two terms, it has the lesser of the two eighths to the farthest of the two terms."
"23781","(23781) Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan: He used to guarantee the shepherd except in the case of death."
"23782","(23782) Waki’ told us, he said: Zakaria told us, on the authority of Amer: He was asked about a shepherd who is liable if he is a wage worker? He said: No."
"23783","(23783) Abu Bakr told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: The shepherd is guaranteed."
"23784","(23784) Hafs told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Amer, who said: The shepherd is not liable."
"23785","(23785) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Al-Muthanna, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, who said: The shepherd is not guaranteed."
"23786","(23786) Qutayba bin Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of Bakr bin Mudar, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: It is not the responsibility of the shepherd. Guarantee"
"23787","(23787) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: I have never seen a narrator except that he included The hired worker, except for a man who hired a man to feed him two mules of grass, and one of them strayed, so he did not guarantee her."
"23788","(23788) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Hassan bin Abi Hamza, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The shepherd is guaranteed, if He was taking care of this person and that person. If he was taking care of you alone, then he is not liable."
"23789","(23789) Abd al-Razzaq told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, who said: The shepherd is not guaranteed."
"23790","(23790) Muhammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Muslim, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Misra, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: If I saw a man who encouraged another man, and he called him to an unjust imam. I bear witness for him: I did not bear witness for him."
"23791","(23791) Qubaysah narrated to us, saying: Sufyan informed us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi and Al-Hakam, they said: If the guardian is appointed He was sworn."
"23792","(23792) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Hammad: Concerning two men who had a mother among them, whom he bought for forty. dinars, so they wanted to sell it to her at a profit, so he gave her fifty dinars, so they fought one of them, then he wanted to He sells it for a profit. He said: He sells it for forty-five dinars. That five is his own profit."
"23793","(23793) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Harith: A man gave alms to his mother with his maidservants, then he married a woman. So he took her to his wife, and they disputed with Shurayh, and he said to his mother: Your son did not give you charity."
"23794","(23794) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim: He used to leave it for his mother, unless he came. By showing that he believed it before he gave it in charity to him."
"23795","(23795) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi: About two men who dealt with money that was between them. So they placed it in the hands of a just man. He said: The property remains as it is with the just man until one of them evaluates the clear evidence."
"23796","(23796) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: A people came to him who were disputing from among The gazelles and they said: Our Sunnah is among us. He said: Your Sunnah is among you."
"23797","(23797) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Abu Asim Al-Ghatfani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi: The mother of a son said to her master: Dance. If your child cries over you, and say: I did not know, then Al-Sha’bi said: If he does not know what Persian means, then it is nothing."
"23798","(23798) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Hayyan, on the authority of Jabir bin Zayd, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: It is not permissible for uncircumcised people to bear witness."
"23799","(23799) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The testimony of an uncircumcised man is not permissible, nor is his prayer accepted, nor is his sacrifice permitted.\n He said: Al-Hasan did not see that."
"23800","(23800) H?? Waki’ told us, he said: Ziyad bin Abi Ziyad told us, he said: I bought a sheep from a man and paid him its price, then I came to arrest her, and the seller said: She wanted to die, so her family slaughtered her, so I argued with him to Sharih, and Sharih said: He refunded the price."
"23801","(23801) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Zakaria narrated to us, on the authority of Amir: He was asked about a man who bought a slave, and he said: The buyer. To the seller: Sell it to me and it is yours to spend. So the slave died in the hands of the seller, and he said: The seller will pay his price."
"23802","(23802) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: If the seller follows up the sale for some price Then he died, so it is part of the seller’s money."
"23803","(23803) Muadh bin Muadh told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If he buys a house for an amount, or for a rent and an amount, that There is no pre-emption in it."
"23804","(23804) Ubaid bin Suhail Al-Ghadani told us, on the authority of Mansour bin Hayyan, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: There was a weaver in His house was the people's yarn, so his house was burned, and the people's yarn was burned, so there remained three kabbaths, so he went with it to Shurayh with him. Two women, and one of them said: He is flirting, and the other said: No, by God, he is flirting, so he left one of them alone and said: Ali What did you do with your ghazal? She said: On the husk of a walnut, and he said to the other: On what did you burn your yarn? She said: On a piece of bread, and he said: O weaver, go and untie this yarn, for if it was on a walnut shell So push him to this, and if he is to break bread, push him to this."
"23805","(23805) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi: Concerning a man, who said: The day I bought so-and-so and he was free, So he bought it and said: He is free."
"23806","(23806) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salamah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: When he said: If you buy this slave So he is free, so he bought it, so he is free."
"23807","(23807) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata: Concerning a man who said: The day he bought so-and-so. So he is free. He said: The day he buys it, he will be freed."
"23808","(23808) Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Abdullah bin Rifa’i Al-Ansari informed me, he said: A man was told: It was mentioned that you wanted to buy so-and-so a child whom they named, so the man said: She is a free woman if you buy her, so Abdullah claimed He asked Saeed bin Al-Musayyab and he said: As for me, I do not see anything in it, but as for Omar bin Abdul-Aziz, he is his father."
"23809","(23809) We told. Al-Qasim and Salem did not permit anyone to divorce or emancipate."
"23810","(23810) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan: Concerning a man who says: If you buy so-and-so, he will be free, or Every female slave whom you have bought over you is free: if he buys any of that, then he has been freed."
"23811","(23811) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah: That a man said to his servant: You belong to him. He said, Al-Shu’bi and Al-Musayyab bin were asked. Rafi’ and Hammad bin Abi Suleiman? They said: He is free."
"23812","(23812) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: If a man says to his servant, or to his female slave: You are freed. You are free. You belong to God, so he is free. If he says: You are the guardian of my son, then he is free."
"23813","(23813) Abu Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Umair: A slave whose master gave permission to perform the sewing, and another slave gave permission In the case of dyeing, he said: Sharih guaranteed them both, so the tailor guaranteed the price of the threads and needles, and the other guaranteed the dyeing and the boiling, etc. The likes of their deeds."
"23814","(23814) Humayd narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: If he was permitted to engage in a type of trade So he deals in a kind other than the one he was permitted to do, so he does not have a religion."
"23815","(23815) Humaid narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan bin Salih: He used to say: If he gives permission to it in one type, then he has given permission to it."
"23816","(23816) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Amr bin Saeed, who said: Ibn Sirin said: Shafi’i is not inherited."
"23817","(23817) I narrated on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Ibn Salem, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Shafi’i is not inherited."
"23818","(23818) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin: He had a debt in his knees, so he used to make up for it. His fines are one to the exclusion of one another."
"23819","(23819) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Al-Harith ibn Umair, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Abu Qalabab, something similar to it, or similar to it"
"23820","(23820) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: There was a shareholder who would not release the seller except from the one whom he knew best. Oh, oh"
"23821","(23821) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Shurayh: Concerning a man who was asking for a man who was in debt and he died. What is required, and Shurayh said: I have made it clear on the basis of his right, and the acquittal is upon the family of the deceased that their companion has been acquitted, or The student’s oath is that he died on the day he died and the right is upon him."
"23822","(23822) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If you sell an item for profit, calculate what you spent on it. And do not count what you spent on yourself."
"23823","(23823) Ishaq bin Mansour narrated to us, he said: Muhammad bin Rashid narrated to us, on the authority of Makhoul: He was reluctant to A man gives another man a dinar and says: Spend it for such-and-such, and you will have whatever is left over."
"23824","(23824) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Rabi’i Al-Ra’i, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz: Concerning a man He sold his slave girl and her two children, then claimed the child, saying: He will return the kingship to him, but the lineage is not proven."
"23825","(23825) Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Abu Shihab told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khalid bin Dinar, on the authority of Al-Harith Al-Ukliy: Concerning the need for cutting the hay to be foddered, he said: If something distracts him from cutting it until he adds more, there is no problem with it."
"23826","(23826) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Tawus: He did not see anything wrong with a man saying To a man if he sells him food: I will pay you back if you die."
"23827","(23827) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan: Concerning a man who said to his servant: Serve me a year. And you are free. He said: He served you for a year and he was free. And if he said: You are free to serve for a year and then the man died: his son served. years after him, and he will be freed from a third of it."
"23828","(23828) Mu’tamir told us, on the authority of his father, he said: A man testified with Omar bin Abdul Aziz as a witness, and he said The person whose testimony is witnessed is not accepted. He said: Why? He said: He does not know who his father is? He said: Bring me evidence other than him."
"23829","(23829) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zuhair al-Absi, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, who said: The child of adultery may lead the prayer, and it is permissible Your testimony"
"23830","(23830) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawwi, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Nafi’ said: It is not permissible for a child of adultery to bear witness."
"23831","(23831) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Hajjaj: that Ibn Abbas used to say: His testimony is permissible."
"23832","(23832) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Sufyan and Zuhair, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of a sheikh from Banu al-Hajjim, who said: I heard Abu Hurairah say: Any man who owes a debt and does not pay it off is like one who owes something sinful."
"23833","(23833) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Abu Makin, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: Any man who owes a debt to Yes, it was easier and he did not fulfill it, so he was destroyed."
"23834","(23834) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad: Concerning a man who says: I have taken, I am satisfied. He said: It is with the choice. What was his condition?"
"23835","(23835) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad: That a man bargained with another man for a garment, and a man said: I will sell you something similar. With such and such, he sold it to him, then he went to the owner of the garment and bought it from him, then brought it to him but he refused to accept it. So he disputed with him to Shurayh and said: We do not find anything more similar to it than it, so he rewarded him."
"23836","(23836) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’: Concerning two men who inherited money and goods that were sold. Was one of them his companion before they were divided? He said: Yes."
"23837","(23837) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He will not sell it until he shares it with him."
"23838","(23838) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The two partners leave."
"23839","(23839) Yahya bin Ali Al-Aslami told us, on the authority of Issa bin Musa, who said: A man asked Al-Hakam about correspondences between Two men, one of whom freed him, and he said: It is only money that he gave to him, and he does not owe anything on it."
"23840","(23840) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri: He did not see any harm in renting out a sufficiency if it was not He gives him dirhams."
"23841","(23841) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Shabak, who said: A man quarreled with his sister to Shuraih over some jewelery on her, and he said : It is my father’s inheritance, so ask her with clear proof that it is hers, and he said: No, rather I ask you with clear proof that it is your father’s."
"23842","(23842) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’: Concerning a man who rents to a worker for a year with his food, He gave him a tax on such-and-such, saying: There is no problem."
"23843","(23843) Al-Dahhak ibn Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, who said: I said to Ata’: I will hire my servant on the condition that I feed him a year, and he year and on the third with the tax of such-and-such? He said: There is no harm in it."
"23844","(23844) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Jarir ibn Hazim, on the authority of Hammad: He disliked a man renting his food."
"23845","(23845) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Mudarib ibn Hazan, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: I was As a reward for my son Ghazwan’s wealth, with my food and the heels of my feet. (Ibn Majah 2445)"
"23846","(23846) Ismail Ibn Aliyya narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Abu al-Muhallab, on the authority of Imran ibn Husayn: That a man had six slaves, so he freed them upon his death, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, cast lots among them. He greeted him and freed two of them and enslaved four. (Muslim 1288, Abu Dawud 3954)"
"23847","(23847) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, he said: Israel informed us, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Mukhtar, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ziyad, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: He cast lots. (Nasa’i 4979)"
"23848","(23848) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Safayya: She cast lots between Hamza and a man in a shroud."
"23849","(23849) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Salih bin Abi Al-Akhdar, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Abi Hisham, on the authority of Malik bin Abdullah Al Khathami, he said: We were sitting with Othman, and he said: Who is here from the people of the Levant? So I stood up and he said: Inform Muawiyah when he seizes a sheep that he should take five shares, and let him record that an share of it is for God. Then let him knock, and let him take it wherever it comes out."
"23850","(23850) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha: that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace, when he traveled he would cast lots among his wives. (Bukhari 2593 and Muslim 2129)"
"23851","(23851) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Wahid bin Ayman narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malikay, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in a similar way. (Bukhari 5211, Muslim 88)"
"23852","(23852) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Aslam Al-Manqari, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr: He cast lots."
"23853","(23853) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Aslam, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, the same."
"23854","(23854) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Khalil Al-Hadrami, on the authority of Zaid Ibn Arqam, he said: A group of people disputed with Ali, he said: He said: Indeed, I am a quarrel between them, he said: So that was mentioned to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He made you laugh until his molars were visible. (Abu Dawud 2263)"
"23855","(23855) Khalid bin Al-Harith narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Aroub, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Khalas, on the authority of Abi Rafi’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah: Two men claimed an animal, but they had no evidence, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded them to do so. And he greeted them to lean on the right."
"23856","(23856) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Usama bin Zaid narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Rafi’, on the authority of Umm Salamah: That the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He said to two men: Ask questions, then strive for the truth, then let each one of you make his companion lawful."
"23857","(23857) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father: that Ibn al-Zubayr cast lots."
"23858","(23858) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ubaidah: He cast lots."
"23859","(23859) Azhar Al-Samman narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: It reached Muhammad ibn Sirin that Omar ibn Abd al-Aziz cast lots, so he said: What I think this is the case with the exception of dividing into divisions."
"23860","(23860) Ibn Idris and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Wasil, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ali: He used to cut Al-Kunf, or he orders its cutting."
"23861","(23861) Azhar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: Muhammad said: I wished that every kinif was cut off, and the first one was a kinif. Abdullah"
"23862","(23862) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Muslim, on the authority of Al-Harith, who said: He was Shurayh and would not let his shadow pass by. The knight thrusts his spear into it, and says: You built on the knight’s spear!"
"23863","(23863) Azhar told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: I asked Al-Hasan about a man who buys on credit? He said: Fear God and eat according to what you have."
"23864","(23864) Azhar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: It was mentioned to Nafi’ that Ibn Umar used to buy things until the end of the month, so he became angry. He said: He used to buy from people he knew and they knew him, so he would extend them a year or two, and he could get a quarter if he wanted. Laba'a made up for them, and Ibn Umar used to make up for it when he was easy."
"23865","(23865) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Al-Hasan: What about a man who spends dinars and gives the person to whom they live counterfeit? He said: There is no harm in replacing it."
"23866","(23866) Waki` narrated to us, saying: And Sufyan said: If it is stolen, return it, and he will be a sharer in the dinars for his share."
"23867","(23867) Waki` narrated to us, saying: I heard Sufyan say: If a man came to a money changer with a dinar and he exchanged it for him With ten dirhams, he received the dinar, but the money changer did not have any dirhams? He said: If he defrauded her to him before they separated, then the sale is permissible, because each one of them is a price for its owner, even if it is Accidentally, the sale was spoiled."
"23868","(23868) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan said: In ten dirhams for seven and a coin, he thought of it, and ten dirhams. With nine dirhams and gold, he saw no harm in it."
"23869","(23869) Waki` narrated to us, saying: I heard Sufyan saying: If he names a person, he is innocent, even if he does not lay his hand."
"23870","(23870) Waki’ told us, I heard Sufyan say: If he says: I am free of every defect, is he innocent?"
"23871","(23871) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Sa’d, who said: I asked Abu Ja’far about a man who bought food from him. So he gives me some of it, then he cuts it off and does not give it to me, so he says: Meaning your food until I finish it? He said: Do not approach this, this open usury."
"23872","(23872) Hafs told us, on the authority of Sulaiman Abi Abdullah, who said: Al-Hasan said: Whoever keeps money from a man, or steals from a man Money, and he wanted to return it to him from where he did not know, so he delivered it to him, so there is no problem."
"23873","(23873) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Sallam bin Abi Dhayal, who said: I asked Al-Hasan about two partners who bought He sold it at a profit for cash and a share, and said: One of them to its owner: Give me my capital, and whatever is left is yours. His good thoughts."
"23874","(23874) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Muhammad, that they both said about a man who sells a weak or sweet product. Then he would give her the rest of it, a sufficient number, but they both hated that."
"23875","(23875) Muhammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala’, on the authority of his followers and Abu Hashim: Concerning a man who bought ten thousand He bought a walnut for thirty dirhams, then he counted it in one jar or two jars, then he counted the rest of it according to what was in the two jars. They said: It is disliked."
"23876","(23876) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a man says to his kings: Indeed, you are a free soul, then he Free"
"23877","(23877) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan: Concerning a man who says to his kings: You are only free. He said: So he said: Al-Hassan: his intention."
"23878","(23878) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, a similar story."
"23879","(23879) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi: Concerning a man whose servant fought another man, and he said: He was only free. Like you, he said: He is free."
"23880","(23880) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, saying: Amr bin Dinar narrated to us, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, who said: A man was wounded on the authority of During the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: Call a doctor for him. They said: O Messenger of God, will he be of no use to him? The doctor? He said: Yes, God, Blessed and Most High, has never sent down a disease without sending down a cure for it. (Ahmad 5/371)"
"23881","(23881) Yunus bin Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Harb bin Maimun narrated to us, saying: I heard Imran the blind, saying: I heard Anas May God be pleased with him, he says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: God, where He created the disease, created the medicine, so they were treated. (Ahmad 3/156)"
"23882","(23882) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi narrated to us, on the authority of Omar bin Saeed bin Abi Hussein, he said: Ata narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hariri, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: God has not sent down a disease except that He has sent it down for it. Healing (Bukhari 5678 and Ibn Majah 3439)"
"23883","(23883) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ziyad ibn Alaqah, on the authority of Usama ibn Sharik, who said: I witnessed the Bedouins asking The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Heal the servants of God, for God did not create a disease without placing a cure with it. The pyramid (Abu Dawud 3851. Tirmidhi 2038)"
"23884","(23884) Hashim bin Al-Qasim narrated to us, saying: Shabib bin Shaybi narrated to us, saying: Ata bin Abi Rabah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: God has not sent down a disease, or He created a disease except when He sent it down, or He created a cure for it, which He taught it to whoever taught it to it, and who ignorantly ignored it, except for the poisonous. They said: Oh. Messenger of God, and what is poison? He said: Death. (Tabarani 92)"
"23885","(23885) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, he said: Abdullah said: No Whether God sends down a disease, or He has not created a disease except that He has sent down a cure for it. Whoever knows it is ignorant of it, and whoever knows it knows it. (Ahmad 1/413)"
"23886","(23886) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Zaid bin Aslam; A man was injured and blood flowed, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called for him two men from Banu Anmar and said: Which of you is better? Then a man said: O Messenger of God, is medicine better than that? He said: Indeed, He who sent down the disease sent down the medicine. (Malik 943)"
"23887","(23887) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Shabib, on the authority of Abu Qalaba; (And it was said: from a gentle person), he said: from a doctor."
"23888","(23888) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Mubarak, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Ka’b, who said: Indeed, God says: I am the one who heals and heals you."
"23889","(23889) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Ibn Abjar, on the authority of Iyad bin Laqit, on the authority of Abu Rimtha, he said: I set out with My father, while I was a boy, came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Then my father said to him: I am a doctor, so show me this. The goods that are on your back. He said: What do you do with them? He said: Cut it off. He said: You are not a doctor, but you are a companion. The doctor is the one who placed it. And someone else said: The one who created it. (Abu Dawud 4204. Tirmidhi 2812)"
"23890","(23890) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He hated drinking all medicines, except milk and honey."
"23891","(23891) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad; He hated drinking paste medicines except something he knew how to do, and if he wanted any of it, he would do it to him. By himself"
"23892","(23892) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abdullah ibn al-Walid, on the authority of Ubaid ibn al-Hasan, on the authority of Ibn Maqil; He hated the evil medicine that, if ingested, kills its owner."
"23893","(23893) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus bin Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of May God bless him and grant him peace from the evil medicine. (Ibn Majah 3459. Ahmad 2/446)"
"23894","(23894) Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, who said: It was said to al-Rabi` ibn Khuthaym In his illness: Should we not call a doctor for you? He said: Wait for me, then he thought and said: {And Aad, and Thamud, and the companions of the land, and many generations between that, and each of them We struck for him. Proverbs: And all of us have purified ourselves, then He mentioned their eagerness for this world and their desire for it. He said: It was a pleasure. And there were doctors among them, but neither the healer nor the healed will perish. The cursed and the denied will perish. By God, do not call for a physician for me."
"23895","(23895) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad; He hated drunkenness, and his father hated it."
"23896","(23896) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, on the authority of Mu’awiyah ibn Qurayh, who said: Abu Darda’ fell ill, so they visited him, and they said: Him: Shall we call a doctor for you? He said: He made me lie down."
"23897","(23897) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They did not see by seeking sight. Valiant, he said: They only disliked it for fear that it would make them weak."
"23898","(23898) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no harm in him walking. Muharram."
"23899","(23899) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was And he said: The best medicine. Al-Laddud, snuff, walking, cupping, and leeches. (Tirmidhi 2053)"
"23900","(23900) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of al-Sha’bi; On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a similar example."
"23901","(23901) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja`far, on the authority of Zur’a ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of a servant of Muammar Al-Taymiyy, on the authority of Asma’ bint Umays, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: What were you walking around with? I said: With shubrum. He said: Hot Jar. Then I tried with senna. He said: If there was anything that could cure death, it was senna. Senna is a cure for death. (Tabarani 3971 Tirmidhi 2081)"
"23902","(23902) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Umm Qays ibn Muhsin, she said: I entered With a son of mine, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I commented on him about his virginity, so he said: Why do you deceive your children? You must adhere to this relationship, you must adhere to this Indian oud, for in it there are seven cures. It is bestowed with it from Virginity, and he gives birth to it from pleurisy. (Bukhari 5692, Muslim 1734)"
"23903","(23903) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered He greeted Umm Salamah when she had a boy with blood coming out of his nostrils, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: What is this? They said: Because of the virginity, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Why do you torture your children? It is enough for one of you to take an Indian portion, rub it with water seven times, then give it to her. He said: So they did it and he was healed. (Ahmad 3/315, Bazzar 3024)"
"23904","(23904) Abdul-Wahhab narrated to us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: The most exemplary of You can treat yourself with cupping and the Arabic treatment for your virgin boys, and do not torture them with innuendo.\n(Bukhari 5696 and Muslim 64)"
"23905","(23905) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: On you. With this black seed, for it contains a cure for every disease. It was said to him: On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: Yes. (Muslim 88. Ahmad 2/268)"
"23906","(23906) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Muslim, on the authority of his leaders, and Matar bin Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraida, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Shawniz contains a cure for every disease. Except the poison. They said: O Messenger of God, what is the poison? He said: Death. (Ahmad 5/346)"
"23907","(23907) Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Israel informed us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Khalid bin Saad, on the authority of Ibn Abi Atiq On the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: You should have this black seed, for it is a cure for Every disease, meaning shingles. (Bukhari 5687. Ahmad 6/138)"
"23908","(23908) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Alqamiya bin Marthad, on the authority of Ali; He used to say the strongest words about the injection."
"23909","(23909) Jarir told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid; He hated her."
"23910","(23910) Sharik and Abbad narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: I will inspect it."
"23911","(23911) A partner told us, on the authority of Jabir, who said: Amer was asked about injections for a fasting person? He said: I hate it for the one who breaks the fast, but how about it for the fasting person?"
"23912","(23912) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: I will certainly examine it."
"23913","(23913) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of his leaders, and Al-Hasan; They both hated the injection."
"23914","(23914) Suwayd bin Amr told us, he said: Abu Awani told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Alqamiya bin Marthad, on the authority of Al-Ma’roor, on the authority of Ali; He hated injections."
"23915","(23915) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: This is a part of the action of the people of Lot. It means the injection."
"23916","(23916) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Mujahid, and Tawoos; They both hated the injection."
"23917","(23917) Jarir told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: There is no harm in it."
"23918","(23918) Sharik told us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Jafar, who said: It is a medicine."
"23919","(23919) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Al-Hakam; He was congested."
"23920","(23920) Omar told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’; He did not see any harm in injections."
"23921","(23921) Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Zuhair told us, on the authority of Mughirah, he said: Abu Ma’shar told me, on the authority of Ibrahim; He did not see any harm in injections."
"23922","(23922) Jarir and Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Rukain, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Hassan, on the authority of his uncle Abd al-Rahman bin Harmala, On the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, disliked wearing amulets. (Ahmad 3971 Hakim 195)"
"23923","(23923) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Isa, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ukaym, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: He who is attached to relationships and entrusts them to them. (Ahmad 4/310, Bayhaqi 351)"
"23924","(23924) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, he said: Abdullah Ali entered His wife was sick, and there was a thread hanging around her neck. He said: What is this? She said: Something I had a ruqyah about for my fever, so he cut it off and said: Indeed, the family of Abraham are free from polytheism."
"23925","(23925) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Ibn Masoud saw something about some of his family that might He clung to him and pulled him away violently, and said: The family of Ibn Masoud is free from polytheism."
"23926","(23926) Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Yunus informed us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Imran bin Al-Husayn, that he saw in the hand of A man shaved his head from scratch and said: What is this? He said: Of weakness. He said: It has only increased your weakness. If you had died while you saw it as beneficial to you, you would have died unnaturally. (Ibn Majah 3531. Ahmad 4/445)"
"23927","(23927) Hushaym told us, saying: Mansour told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Imran bin Al-Husayn; Like that"
"23928","(23928) Ali ibn Mushir told us, on the authority of Yazid, he said: Zayd ibn Wahhab informed me, he said: His hoe set off for... A man from Nakha was preparing his camel, so he went off and I went with him, so he went in to him and I went in with him. He touched his upper arm and saw a thread in it. So he took it and cut it, then said: If you had died with this on your arm, I would not have prayed for you."
"23929","(23929) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: Ali entered upon a man. He came back and found a thread on his upper arm. He said: So he said: What is this? He said: A thread on which a ruqyah was performed for me, so he cut it, then said: If you had died, I would not have prayed over you."
"23930","(23930) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Al-Muhajir, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah; He disliked commenting on any part of the Qur’an."
"23931","(23931) Shababi told us, he said: Laith bin Saad told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Abu Al-Khair, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, He said: The placement of an amulet on a person or a child is shirk."
"23932","(23932) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Imran, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: Whoever is attached to a relationship and is entrusted with it."
"23933","(23933) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Abraham, he said: They used to hate all amulets, From the Qur’an and other than the Qur’an."
"23934","(23934) Hushaym told us, saying: Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He hated that."
"23935","(23935) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, he said: I said to Abraham: I attach to your arm these verses: {O Fire. Be coolness and peace upon Abraham} from the fever that was in me? He thought that"
"23936","(23936) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Hilal, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: Whoever wears amulets and performs ruqyahs, then he is a part of polytheism upon his people."
"23937","(23937) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They used to hate amulets and incantations. And publishing."
"23938","(23938) Abdul narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Suqi; Sa`id bin Jubayr saw a man going around the Kaaba with a bead around his neck, so he cut it."
"23939","(23939) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: Whoever cuts an amulet on behalf of a person is like a just person. Neck"
"23940","(23940) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Waqi’ ibn Sahban, who said: Abdullah said: Whoever hangs something He has been entrusted to Him."
"23941","(23941) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Shihab, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, he said: He had a brother with him, he said: So he said He has a man: Is it ruqyah for you from her? He said: I have no need for ruqyah."
"23942","(23942) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibrahim; He disliked the sanctuary for children, and he said: They enter the private rooms therein."
"23943","(23943) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hashim bin Hashim, who said: I heard Aamir bin Saad bin Abi Waqqas saying: I heard Saad He says: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Whoever starts the morning with seven Ajwa dates, that will not harm him. Today is poison, and there is no magic. (Bukhari 5445. Muslim 154)"
"23944","(23944) Yazeed told us, on the authority of Abbad bin Mansour, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Ajwa is from heaven, and it is a cure for poison. (Tirmidhi 2068. Ahmad 3/48)"
"23945","(23945) Ibn Numayr told us, he said: Hisham bin Urwa told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha; She used to order those who were at work, or at work, to eat seven dates on an empty stomach, seven early mornings."
"23946","(23946) Khaled bin Mukhlid narrated to us, saying: Suleiman bin Bilal narrated to us, saying: Sharik bin Abdullah bin Abi Nimr narrated to us. On the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abi Atiq, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Concerning The high Ajwa is a cure or: it is a cure at the beginning of the morning on an empty stomach. (Muslim 1619. An-Nasa’i 6714)"
"23947","(23947) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Anas bin Sirin, on the authority of Anas; The mother of Sulaym gave birth to a boy, and Abu Talha said to him: Carry him until you bring him to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He was brought to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he sent some dates with him. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, took him and said: Is there anything with him? They said: Yes, dates, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, took them and chewed them, then took from his mouth and put them in his mouth. Al-Sabiya, then he shaped it with him and named him Abdullah. (Bukhari 5470, Muslim 1689)"
"23948","(23948) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Burayd bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Burda, on the authority of Abu Musa, who said: A boy was born to me. So I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he named him Ibrahim, and he seasoned him with a date. (Bukhari 6198 and Muslim 24)"
"23949","(23949) Khalid bin Mukhlid told us, on the authority of Ibn Mushir, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Asma bint Abi Bakr; She brought Ibn al-Zubayr to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when she gave birth to him, and they asked for dates until they found them and he flavored them. With it, the first thing that entered his stomach was the saliva of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Bukhari 3909, Muslim 1691)"
"23950","(23950) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to bring children and bless them and be kind to them. (Bukhari 6002, Muslim 1691)"
"23951","(23951) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Muslim, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Mundakir, on the authority of Jabir, he said: I heard The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: You should use clothing when sleeping, for it strengthens eyesight and makes hair grow.\n(Ibn Majah 3496)"
"23952","(23952) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khathim, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The best of your eyes is antimony, it clears sight. And hair grows."
"23953","(23953) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Abdul Hamid bin Jafar, on the authority of Imran bin Abi Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, applies kohl with antimony, and applies kohl to the right hand three times, and to the left hand two times. (Ibn Saad 484)"
"23954","(23954) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Hafsa, on the authority of Anas; He used to apply kohl three times in each eye."
"23955","(23955) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; He used to apply kohl to two women in one case, two women in another case, and one in between."
"23956","(23956) Yazeed told us, on the authority of Abbad bin Mansour, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: It was for the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, used kohl to apply kohl to each eye three times. (Tirmidhi 2048. Ibn Majah 3499)"
"23957","(23957) Shababah narrated to us, saying: Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Alqamiya bin Wa’il, on the authority of his father; That a man from Ja`fi, called Suwayd bin Tariq, asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about alcohol? So he forbade it and said: O Messenger of God, we only make it as a medicine. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: It is A disease but not a cure."
"23958","(23958) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Wael; A man became jaundiced, and he was described as drunk, so he asked Abdullah about that? He said: God did not make your cure for what He has forbidden to you."
"23959","(23959) Khalaf bin Khalifa told us, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: It was owned by Ibn Omar Bakhtiyya, and it She fell ill, and it was prescribed for me to treat her with wine, so I treated her, then I said to Ibn Umar: They prescribed for me to treat her. With wine, he said: So you did? I said: No, and I had done so. He said: If you had done so, I would have punished you."
"23960","(23960) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Ibn Amir and Ibn Ziyad said: I will not bring anyone to drink wine to a child except that I will flog him. Ibn Aoun said: And my memorizer: Ibn Ziyad."
"23961","(23961) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar; He hated to give the animals wine to drink."
"23962","(23962) Abdul Rahim told us, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Abraham; He hated to be treated with wine, the blood of a dream, or fire."
"23963","(23963) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Atiyya, he said: I heard Al-Hasan being asked about a boy who complained. You were described. Has a drop of wine? He said: No."
"23964","(23964) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; Aisha used to say: Whoever treats himself with wine, God will not cure him."
"23965","(23965) Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Amir, who said: Ibn Amir said: Whoever makes a child drink wine, we will flog him. The one who gave him water."
"23966","(23966) Abdou narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim; Ibn Umar disliked treating the anus of camels with wine."
"23967","(23967) Ja’far bin Aoun narrated to us, saying: Ayman bin Nabul narrated to us, on the authority of Umm Kulthum ibn Amr, on the authority of Aisha, She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: You must do what is hateful and beneficial. With his hand, he washes the stomach of one of you just as one of you washes his face of dirt, and whenever anyone complains of People, the spear will not stay on the fire until it destroys one of its ends. (Tirmidhi 2039. Ahmad 6/32)"
"23968","(23968) Abdou bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Omar, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was He, peace and blessings be upon him, cups the bottom of the wolf, and calls it a savior."
"23969","(23969) Aswad bin Amir told us, he said: Jarir bin Hazim told us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace three times, upon the deceitful ones, and one upon the eldest. (Tirmidhi 2051, Abu Dawud 3856)"
"23970","(23970) Khaled bin Mukhlid told us, he said: Suleiman bin Bilal told us, he said: Alqamih bin Abi Alqamih told me, he said: I heard Abd al-Rahman al-Araj saying: I heard Abd Allah ibn Buhna saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was cupped with his beard. A camel in ihram, in the middle of its head. (Bukhari 1836; Ibn Majah 3481)"
"23971","(23971) Yazid bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Yahya bin Yazid narrated to us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Saar; The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, performed cupping in a place on the road to Mecca, with a device called a camel’s jaw, while he was in ihram. His head"
"23972","(23972) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Hassan bin Salih, on the authority of Mansour, who said: I said to Mujahid: The Messenger of God was cupped. May God bless him and grant him peace? He said: Except that his leg was broken and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cupped it."
"23973","(23973) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had cupping while he was in ihram, and his head was affected by some harm he had caused. (Bukhari 5699, Abu Dawud 1832)"
"23974","(23974) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas said: If her child is difficult for the woman, then she should write these two verses and words on a sheet of paper, then she should wash herself. Then you are given to drink of it: In the name of God, to whom there is no god but Him, the Forbearing, the Most Generous. Glory be to God, Lord of the seven heavens and Lord of the Great Throne: {As if on the day they saw it they had not tarried except for the evening or the afternoon}, {As if on the day they saw it they had been promised They did not remain but an hour of the day of conveyance, so all will be destroyed except the disobedient people.}"
"23975","(23975) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Aisha; She did not see any harm in him immersing himself in water and then pouring it on the sick person."
"23976","(23976) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalabab (h) and Laith, on the authority of Mujahid; They did not see any harm in writing a verse from the Qur’an and then giving it to drink for the one who was frightened."
"23977","(23977) Hushaym told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, he said: he told me who saw Saeed bin Jubayr writing The spell is for the one who came to it. Hajjaj said: And I asked Ata? He said: We have not heard of his hatred except from you, the people of Iraq."
"23978","(23978) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of his people, he said: His leaders told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin al-Musayyab, he said: I asked him about Al-Nashr, so he commanded me to do so. I said: Should I narrate it on your authority? He said: Yes."
"23979","(23979) Yazeed told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad; The Mother of the Believers, Aisha, was asked about the revelation? She said: What do you do with this? This is the Euphrates next to you, and one of you will soak in it seven times, and he will meet the Jiraiya."
"23980","(23980) Hushaym told us, saying: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Ibrahim; He was asked about a man who used to write down verses from the Qur’an out of fear on his cup, and the sick person would give him something to drink? He thought that"
"23981","(23981) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Atiyya, he said: I heard Al-Hasan and he was asked about the publication? He said: Magic."
"23982","(23982) Ibn Uyaynah and Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Abu Raji, who said: I asked Al-Hasan about publishing? Then he mentioned to me on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: It is the work of Satan. (Bazzar 3034)"
"23983","(23983) Utham bin Ali told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: Who afflicted him? Whether it is a plague, or poison, or magic, let him come to the Euphrates, face the stream, and immerse himself in it seven times."
"23984","(23984) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Yazid ibn Hayyan, on the authority of Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: The Prophet’s prayers May God bless him and grant him peace. A man from among the Jews complained. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, complained about this for several days, so Gabriel came to him. He said: Such-and-such a Jewish man bewitched you and made a marriage contract for you, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent to her. So he took it out, brought it, and whenever he untied it, he felt light for it. He said: Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, stood up. It is as if he had been loosened from a sash. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, never mentioned that Jew, nor did he ever see him in his face. (Ahmad 4/367, Hakim 360)"
"23985","(23985) Abdullah bin Numir told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, bewitched May the peace and blessings of God be upon him. He was a Jew from the Jews of Banu Zurayq, called Labid bin Al-Aasm. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was May God bless him and grant him peace, it seems to him that he is doing something and he is not doing it, even if it is the same day, or One night, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called, then made supplication, then said: O Aisha, do you feel that God has Did he give me a fatwa regarding what you asked for a fatwa about? Two men came to me, and one of them sat at my head, and the other at my feet, and the one at my head said to the one at my feet, Or the one at my feet to the one at my head: What is the man’s pain? They said: He was healed. He said: Who had healed him? He said: Labid bin Al-Aasm. He said: About what? He said: In the comb and combs, and the dryness of his male hair. He said: Where is he? He said: In the well of Dhu Arwan. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to it among some of his companions, then he came and said: Aisha, as if her water was infused with henna, and as if her palm trees were the heads of the devils. He said: So I said: O Messenger of God, is it not? Did you take it out? He said: No, as for me, God has healed me, and I hate to incite people to do evil because of him, so he commanded that I be buried, and I was buried. (Bukhari 3175, Muslim 1719)"
"23986","(23986) Shababih narrated to us, he said: Laith bin Saad narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said : When Khaybar was conquered, a tea containing poison was given to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Gather together for me those of the Jews who are here, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to them: Did you make this tea poison? They said: Yes. He said: What made you do that? They said: We wanted to find relief from you if you were a liar, and if you were a prophet he would not harm you. (Bukhari 3169, Abu Dawud 4501)"
"23987","(23987) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’; He saw no harm in coming to the one who was taken on behalf of his family, or the one who was bewitched, who was divorced from him."
"23988","(23988) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, he said: I asked Ata’ Al-Khurasani about the taken and the enchanted. It comes from He divorces him? He said: There is no harm in that if he is forced to do so."
"23989","(23989) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: I told him: A man who obtained medicine through magic. Is it permissible for him? He said: Yes, whoever is able to benefit his brother, let him do so."
"23990","(23990) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Hajjaj Al-Sawwaf, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Hilal bin Abi Maymunah, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yassar, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Al-Hakam Al-Sulami, who said: I said: O Messenger of God, it is a hadith of a covenant. For my sake, and God has brought Islam, and among us are men who go to the soothsayers. He said: So do not go to them. (Muslim 381, Abu Dawud 927)"
"23991","(23991) Abu Muawiyah told us, he said: Al-Shaybani told us, on the authority of Jami’ bin Shaddad, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Hilal, he said: He said: Ali: Indeed, these fortune-tellers are the soothsayers of the non-Arabs, so whoever goes to a soothsayer and believes in what he says, then he is innocent of what God has revealed to him. Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"23992","(23992) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: A dirham of a min is better. From the heart of a man comes the fortune teller."
"23993","(23993) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Bakr, on the authority of Abu Masoud; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the use of a soothsayer."
"23994","(23994) Yahya bin Adam and Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Hubayra, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: Whoever goes to a magician, or a soothsayer, or a fortune-teller, and he believes what he says, has disbelieved in what God has revealed to him. Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"23995","(23995) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, he said: Did you ask her about ruqyah for fever? She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, permitted the ruqyah to be performed by anyone with a fever. (Bukhari 5741, Muslim 1724)"
"23996","(23996) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, on the authority of the ruqyah, and the family of Amr ibn Hazm had a ruqyah with which they recited a ruqyah from a scorpion. He said: So they came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. So they presented it to him and said: You have forbidden ruqyah. So he said: Who among you is able to benefit his brother? Let him do it. (Muslim 1726. Ahmad 3/315)"
"23997","(23997) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of some of the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: There is no ruqyah except for an eye or a fever. (Abu Dawud 3880, Tirmidhi 2057)"
"23998","(23998) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: I was stung by a scorpion, and blood dripped from my nostrils. The black separated me and I was healed."
"23999","(23999) Khalaf bin Khalifa told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He did not see any harm in the telegram of fever."
"24000","(24000) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: He permitted ruqyah against fever, ants, and the soul."
"24001","(24001) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amara, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Muhammad; Khalidah bint Anas, the mother of Banu Hazm al-Sa’idi, came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and offered him a ruqyah. So he commanded her to do so."
"24002","(24002) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Yusuf bin Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Anas said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave permission for ruqyah against the evil eye and fever. (Muslim 1725. Tirmidhi 2056)"
"24003","(24003) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Amer, who said: Ibn Masoud saw on his son a shin of fever, So he cut it off and said: There is no ruqyah except from an eye or a fever."
"24004","(24004) Ali bin Musir told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He was cast as a luminary from the scorpion."
"24005","(24005) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: The family of lions had a ruqyah which they used to qirqan. With it in the pre-Islamic period of fever, he said: Then the lions showed it to Aisha, he said: So she ordered them to perform ruqyah with it, he said: Aisha said: There is no ruqyah except from an eye or a fever."
"24006","(24006) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Sulaiman ibn Abi Hathama; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to his grandmother, Al-Shifa’ bint Abdullah: Teach Hafsa your ruqyah, Abu Bishr said. Meaning: Ismail Ibn Aliyah: So I said to Muhammad: What was your ruqyah? He said: The ant ruqyah. (Ahmad 6/286)"
"24007","(24007) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Yusuf bin Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Anas said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave permission to perform ruqyah for ants."
"24008","(24008) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz bin Omar narrated to us, saying: Salih bin Kaysan narrated to me, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Sulaiman bin Abi Hathamiah, that Al-Shifa’, the son of Abdullah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon me. I was sitting with Hafsa bint Omar, and he said: What prevents you from teaching this ruqyah to the ant as you taught her? Writing (Abu Dawud 3883. Ahmad 372)"
"24009","(24009) Uqba bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Shu’abi, on the authority of Abu Ismah, he said: I asked Saeed bin Al-Musayyab about exorcism? He said: There is no harm in it if it is in a human body."
"24010","(24010) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; In the case of a menstruating woman, she must perform a spell. He said: If it is of human skin, then she should remove it, but if there is silver on his shin, If you wish, you may place it, and if you wish, you may not place it."
"24011","(24011) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Thawair, who said: Mujahid used to write spells for people and hang them up. May God bless you"
"24012","(24012) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Ja`far, on the authority of his father; He did not see any harm in writing the Qur’an on a human being and then hanging it on it."
"24013","(24013) Abduh narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: If one of you is startled in his sleep, let him say: I seek refuge in the perfect words of God from His wrath. And his punishment is evil, and from the evil of his servants, and from the evil of the devils and what they attend. Abdullah used to teach her to his children who caught her. Some of them, and whoever did not realize it, wrote it down and attached it to him. (Abu Dawud 3889. Tirmidhi 3528)"
"24014","(24014) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Muslim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; He saw no harm in anything from the Qur’an."
"24015","(24015) Affan told us, he said: Wahib told us, he said: Ayoub told us; He saw a thread on the arm of Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah bin Omar."
"24016","(24016) Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Hassan told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, he said: There is no harm in suspending the Qur’an."
"24017","(24017) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, on the authority of Aban bin Thalab, on the authority of Yunus bin Khabab, who said: I asked Abu Jafar about Is the spell applied to boys? So he made it permissible."
"24018","(24018) Ishaq Al-Azraq told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak; He did not see any harm in a man hanging something from the Book of God, if he put it on when washing and defecating."
"24019","(24019) Abd al-Rahim told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of al-Minhal ibn Amr, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ali, on the authority of Ali, he said: Between us The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was praying one night, and he put his hand on the ground, and a scorpion stung him, so he ate it. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took off his sandals and killed her. When he left, he said: May God curse the scorpion. Do not leave a woman praying, or anyone else. Or a prophet, and no one else. Then he called for salt and water and put it in a vessel, then he poured it on his finger where it had stung. And He anoints her and seeks refuge in her with the two exorcists. (Tabarani 830)"
"24020","(24020) Abdul Rahim told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, he said: He used to perform ruqyah. With donkeys."
"24021","(24021) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of al-Qaqa`, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The ruqyah of a scorpion: its horns are salted. Bahr Qafta. (Tabarani 8681)"
"24022","(24022) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Qaqa’, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, he said: I showed it to Aisha. She said: These are covenants."
"24023","(24023) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Tariq bin Abi Makhashin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said : A man was brought to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who had been stung by a scorpion, and he said: But if he had said: I seek refuge in the perfect words of God Of the evil of what He created, He did not bite, nor did He harm Him. (Muslim 2081, Ibn Hibban 1021)"
"24024","(24024) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to perform ruqyahs, and they disliked blowing into the mouth. Ruqyah"
"24025","(24025) Ar’arah ibn al-Barand narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Hazzaz, who said: I entered upon al-Dahhak while he was in pain, so I said: No. I seek refuge in you, O Abu Muhammad? He said: Yes, and do not blow it. He said: So I sought refuge with him with the two refuges."
"24026","(24026) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Ayyub, he said: Ikrimah said: I hate to say about ruqyah, in the name of God, Ugh"
"24027","(24027) Abu Qatn told us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Al-Hakam, and Hammad; They both hated to spit on ruqyah."
"24028","(24028) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Hatib, who said: I approached a pot of ours and my hands burned, so it came. My mother took me to a sheikh in Al-Batha’i, and she said: This is Muhammad, his hand has been burned, so he started blowing on her and talking. With words that I do not remember, when he was in the command of Othman, I said: Who is the sheikh to whom you brought? She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Ahmad 3/259. Ibn Hibban 2976)"
"24029","(24029) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Abdul Aziz bin Omar told me, he said: A man from Banu Salman bin Saad told me. On the authority of his mother; Her maternal uncle Habib bin Fuwayk told her that his father took him to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and helped him. Two white spots, he could not see anything in them, so he asked him what had happened to him? So he informed him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, blew into his eyes, and I saw him inserting the thread into the needle. He is eighty years old, and his eyes are white. (Tabarani 3546)"
"24030","(24030) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Malik bin Anas, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Aisha; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to blow on ruqyah. (Bukhari 1311, Muslim 1723)"
"24031","(24031) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: Othman bin Hakim narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman bin Abd al-Aziz informed me, on the authority of Ali bin Murrah said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a woman raising a young boy to him, and he made him his son. Then he opened his mouth and blew into it. (Hakim 617)"
"24032","(24032) Hafs told us, on the authority of Othman bin Qais, on the authority of Qais bin Muhammad bin Al-Ash’ath, he said: Take me to Aisha. And there was evil in my eyes, you separated me and blew me away."
"24033","(24033) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: I asked Muhammad about a ruqyah that is used to blow on it? He said: I don't know of any harm in it."
"24034","(24034) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ziyad bin Thuwaib, on the authority of Abu Hariri, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to me while I was complaining, and he said: Shall I not perform a ruqyah on you? Gabriel taught me, in the name of God, I incite you, and God will heal you from every affliction that harms you, and from the evil of blowing in The knot, and from the evil of the envier when he envies. (Ahmad 2/446, Ibn Majah 3524)"
"24035","(24035) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abd Rabbah, on the authority of Umar, on the authority of Aisha; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say to a sick person when he touched a slug with his finger: In the name of God, the soil of our land. With the saliva of one another, our sick will be healed, with the permission of our Lord.\n(Bukhari 5745. Muslim 1724)"
"24036","(24036) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was May God bless him and grant him peace, he seeks refuge in these words: Remove the affliction, Lord of people, and heal, and you are the healer. There is no cure except your healing. A cure that does not leave an illness behind. She said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, became ill due to the illness in which he died, I took With his hand, I started to wipe it and say it. She said: Then he took his hand from mine and said: O God, forgive me, and join me with the comrade. The highest, she said: This was the last I heard of his words. (Muslim 1722 and Ibn Majah 1619)"
"24037","(24037) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bā, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Salamah, on the authority of Ali, who said: I complained, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to me and I was saying: If my time has come, then have mercy on me, even if it is late. So heal me, or make me well, and if it is a trial, then give me patience. He said: Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: How did you say? He said: So I told him, he said: So he wiped me with his hand, then said: Oh God, heal him, or make him well, and I never complained of that pain after that. (Tirmidhi 3544, Ibn Hibban 6940)"
"24038","(24038) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever enters upon a sick person and his death is not present, then he says: I ask God Almighty, my Lord. The Great Throne is to heal you, seven times, and you are healed. (Ahmad 1/239, Abu Dawud 3099)"
"24039","(24039) Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, he said: Umair ibn Hani informed me, he said: I heard Junada bin Abi Umayyah says: I heard Ubad bin Al-Samit narrating on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Indeed, Gabriel recited the incantation for you while he was weak, and said: In the name of God, I recite the incantation for you, from every disease that harms you, from every envier when he envies. And from every eye, and the name of God will heal you. (Ahmad 5/323, Ibn Hibban 953)"
"24040","(24040) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was And when he entered upon a sick person, he greeted him and said: Remove the affliction, Lord of people, and heal you, you are the healer. There is no cure except your recovery. (Tirmidhi 3565)"
"24041","(24041) Muhammad bin Bishr al-Abdi narrated to us, saying: Zakaria narrated to us, saying: Simak narrated to me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Hatib, He said: I took some pot for us and my hands burned, so my mother took me to a man sitting in the cemetery, and she said: O Messenger of God, He said: At your service and my happiness. Then she brought me closer to him, and he started blowing his throat and speaking words that I do not know what they were, so I asked my mother. After that: What was he saying? She said: He used to say: Remove the affliction, Lord of people, and heal you, you are the healer, there is no healer but you.\n(Ibn Saad 650)"
"24042","(24042) Ahmad bin Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Abu Shihab narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Abu Nadhru, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, complained, and Gabriel comforted him and said: In the name of God, I offer you ruqyah, of all things. He harms you, from every envier and evil eye, and God will heal you. (Muslim 1718, Tirmidhi 982)"
"24043","(24043) Ali told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Minhal, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to seek refuge with Al-Hassan and Al-Hussein, saying: I seek refuge with you with the perfect words of God, from Every devil and a wild beast, and from every evil eye a mother, and he says, This is how Abraham used to seek refuge with his son Ishmael. And Isaac\n(Tirmidhi 2060 and Abu Dawud 4704)"
"24044","(24044) Ubaidah bin Hamid told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Manhal, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace; Like it, or something similar."
"24045","(24045) Zaid bin Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Ismail bin Abi Habib, he said: Dawud bin Al-Husayn, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to teach us about pain. All of them and from fever this supplication: In the name of God the Great, I seek refuge in God Almighty, from the evil of every race of disgrace, and from the evil of heat Fire (Tirmidhi 2075, Ibn Majah 3526)"
"24046","(24046) Al-Hasan bin Musa narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salma narrated to us, on the authority of Farqad Al-Sabkhi, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; A woman brought her son to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, this is his son. Madness, and he took him at our dinner and lunch, so he was malicious. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wiped his chest. He called for him, and a snake yelped, and it came out from his belly like a black puppy. (Ahmad 1/239. Tabarani 12)"
"24047","(24047) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa`id, on the authority of Amra Ibn Abd al-Rahman, she said: She complained Aisha, the Mother of the Believers, and Abu Bakr entered upon her while she was a Jew, and he said: Perform ruqyah for her according to the Book of God."
"24048","(24048) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Fudayl bin Amr, who said: A man came to Ali and said: So-and-so doubted. He said: Would you be pleased that he was healed? He said: Yes, he said: Say, O Forbearing, O Generous, heal so-and-so."
